{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cxb3smxNqg6UY2xCPpKDke","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — StructFuse\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main\n5\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n6\t\n7\t## Core Claims (3)\n8\t\n9\t1. **Simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement for contrastive code retrieval at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies.** CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025) argues non-differentiable embedding negatives are \"slow and ineffective\" compared to gradient-based methods — our results show that in structural code retrieval, simple embedding-distance mining yields (pilot: +1.6–2.0pp; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; final range pending s42/s44 completion) R@1 over random baselines across two decoder-only encoders with distinct pretraining corpora and representation geometries (Qwen2.5-Coder-3B, StarCoder2-3B), without requiring gradient-based mechanisms.\n10\t\n11\t2. **[Exploratory observation] Structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives interact with encoder representation geometry, but do not consistently outperform embedding mining.** Pilot data shows dataflow < embedding on both encoders (Qwen: -1.2pp, StarCoder: -1.0pp R@1 vs embedding). The interaction pattern — Qwen (saturated, pos_sim > 0.98) shows smaller gap than StarCoder (healthy, pos_sim ~ 0.80) — suggests representation geometry mediates strategy effectiveness. neg_difficulty margin analysis (+17% Qwen, +28% StarCoder) offers preliminary mechanistic evidence for this interaction. Pending: multi-seed confirmation + plan_005 stratified analysis + plan_015 dynamic mining control. This is reported as an observation with mechanistic hypothesis, not an established finding.\n12\t\n13\t3. **Scope-bounded inter-procedural data-flow analysis via CodeQL provides a practical pipeline for computing structural connectivity at scale.** 0% timeout, 78% connected-not-gold rate (Z%), 123/131 repos with output at full scale. [Dream [M][W] flag: this is supporting methodology, not a primary research contribution. Drop speculative generalization claims (molecular networks, etc.) — no evidence. Frame as practical tool that enables the study, not a standalone contribution.]\n14\t\n15\t## Story Spine\n16\t\n17\t- **Problem**: Repo-level code repair requires selecting relevant files from large codebases. Current retrievers rely on text similarity alone, but lexical similarity ≠ structural relevance. Hard negative mining is the standard approach to improve contrastive retrievers, yet the field lacks systematic understanding of what negative selection strategies work for code and why.\n18\t\n19\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**:\n20\t  - Text-based retrieval (SweRank, SWE-Fixer): blind to structural dependencies\n21\t  - Graph-guided at inference (LocAgent, RANGER, CodexGraph): structural graphs at inference only, no training signal\n22\t  - ARISE: data-flow but intra-procedural only (no call boundary crossing), runtime tool calls only\n23\t  - CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025): argues gradient-based hard negative methods outperform non-differentiable embedding negatives — but does not test simple static embedding-distance mining in structural code retrieval settings\n24\t  - Gap: no systematic study comparing negative mining strategies with proper controls, and no mechanistic explanation for when/why each strategy works\n25\t\n26\t- **Our contribution**: A systematic analysis of hard negative mining strategies for contrastive code retrieval. We (1) show that simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies, (2) [exploratory] observe that structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives interact with encoder representation geometry and offer preliminary mechanistic analysis of when/why different strategies may yield different outcomes, and (3) validate findings on downstream SWE-bench task evaluation.\n27\t\n28\t- **Headline result template**: \"Simple static embedding-distance mining improves code retrieval in pilot and initial M2 seed (pilot: +1.6–2.0pp; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; consistency across remaining seeds pending; 2 encoders), providing a reliable zero-cost baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies. Structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives show encoder-dependent interaction patterns — representation geometry analysis via negative difficulty offers a candidate mechanistic explanation for when different mining strategies are effective.\"\n29\t\n30\t## Core Insight\n31\t\n32\tOur pilot data suggests that the effectiveness of hard negative mining strategies may depend on the encoder's representation geometry — a hypothesis derived from two encoders and requiring broader validation. The three strategies explore different dimensions of difficulty: (1) random — no signal baseline; (2) embedding-distance — semantic similarity via pretrained encoder cosine similarity; (3) dataflow-aware — structural filtering (CodeQL-connected files) + lexical similarity (BM25 top-K ranking). When the pretrained space is saturated (high pos_sim → low margin between positive and negative), the encoder needs harder negatives from an orthogonal signal dimension (structure + lexical). When the space has healthy separation, embedding-distance mining alone captures sufficient difficulty gradient. This encoder-strategy interaction, if confirmed, could help explain contradictory findings in prior work.\n33\t\n34\t## Dual-Pillar Motivation\n35\t\n36\t1. **Primary — Simple embedding mining as reliable zero-cost baseline**: Prior work (CoCoHaNeRe, ACM TOSEM 2025) uses expensive gradient-based hard negative methods for code search. Our controlled comparison shows simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline and isolating the effect of each strategy.\n37\t2. **Secondary — Mechanistic explanation via representation geometry**: neg_difficulty analysis (margin distribution × strategy × encoder) offers preliminary explanatory depth beyond empirical comparison, offering a candidate heuristic (pos_sim threshold) that, if validated on more encoders, could help practitioners select strategies without exhaustive experiments.\n38\t\n39\t## Formal Definition\n40\t\n41\tGiven retrieval domain D, structural graph G, query q:\n42\t**structure-grounded hard negative** = argmax_{x ∈ D : ¬reachable_G(x,q) ∧ x ∉ gold(q)} BM25(q, x)\n43\t\n44\tThe structural graph is externally fixed and does not update with the encoder (drift-immune). Negatives are selected from structurally unreachable files (i.e., x ∉ R_G(q), not connected via CodeQL data-flow to the query), ranked by BM25 (lexical similarity).\n45\t\n46\t## Title Options\n47\t\n48\t- Primary: \"What Makes Hard Negatives Work for Code Retrieval? A Systematic Study of Mining Strategies and Representation Geometry\"\n49\t- Alternative: \"Static Embedding Negatives as a Zero-Cost Baseline for Contrastive Code Retrieval\" [contingent: activate only if M2 dataflow conditional benefit confirmed across encoders]\n50\t- Backup: \"Simple Embedding Mining Suffices: A Zero-Cost Baseline for Hard Negative Mining in Code Retrieval\"\n51\t\n52\t## Venue Fit\n53\t\n54\t1. **EMNLP Main fit**: Empirical analysis + mechanistic insight papers are a strong EMNLP archetype (cf. \"Do Language Models...\" papers). Contribution is understanding, not just a new method.\n55\t2. **NLP audience**: Frame as contrastive learning methodology with code as instantiation. Representation geometry analysis generalizes beyond code.\n56\t3. **Against \"incremental\" criticism**: Paper demonstrates a reliable zero-cost baseline + offers preliminary mechanistic analysis of strategy × encoder interaction + validates on downstream task. Three contributions, not one marginal improvement.\n57\t\n58\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n59\t\n60\t| Concern | Response | Evidence |\n61\t|---------|----------|----------|\n62\t| Only 2 encoders — can you generalize? | n=2 is minimum for interaction claim; we frame as observation with mechanism, not universal law; two decoder-only encoders with distinct pretraining (Fill vs FIM) and representation geometry (pos_sim 0.99 vs 0.80) provide meaningful variation | plan_013 (done), m2_full runs |\n63\t| BM25 vs true embedding negatives? | Run BM25 negatives to empirically compare with embedding-distance mining, grounding the comparison against CoCoHaNeRe's gradient-based premise | plan_018 |\n64\t| Pool size sensitivity? | Evaluate at pool {50, 100, 200, 500} to confirm strategy rankings hold at realistic sizes | plan_019 |\n65\t| Stratified by structural data availability? | Report per-stratum R@1 for 34% with structural data vs 66% fallback | plan_005 (extended) |\n66\t| Temperature regime specificity | Ablate τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2} | plan_014 |\n67\t| No downstream task evaluation | SWE-bench Lite end-to-end with LLM agent | plan_003 |\n68\t| Static vs dynamic mining confound | Clarify mining is static; add dynamic baseline | plan_015 |\n69\t| CodeQL scalability at larger scale | 0% timeout, 78% Z%, 123 repos; m1_reextract_v2 adds more | plan_006 (done) |\n70\t| Why not compare inference-time graph methods? | Complementary: they navigate at inference, we mine at training. Discuss relationship. | plan_017 |\n71\t| Single benchmark | Add RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval | plan_004 |\n72\t| Statistical significance | Bootstrap 95% CI for all comparisons; full M2 = 9 seeds × 3 strategies × 2 encoders | plan_016, m2_full |\n73\t| \"Complementary signal\" overstatement | Temper: \"conditionally beneficial\" not \"always complementary\" | Writing discipline |\n74\t| Missing related work | RepoFusion, GRACE, GraphCodeBERT, ANCE, curriculum HN mining | Writing task |\n75\t\n76\t## Evidence Status\n77\t\n78\t### Confirmed findings (basis for claims):\n79\t- D017: True embedding mining helps (pilot: +2.0pp Qwen, +1.6pp StarCoder; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; final range pending s42/s44 completion) — establishes reliable zero-cost baseline\n80\t- D021/neg_difficulty: Qwen pos_sim=0.9855 (saturated), StarCoder pos_sim=0.7985 (healthy); margin differential is consistent with hypothesized strategy interaction\n81\t- m2_embed_verify (pilot): 3-strategy comparison is consistent with pilot ranking (embedding > random, dataflow conditional)\n82\t- plan_013 (StarCoder pilot): Consistent with cross-encoder pattern — embedding helps both, dataflow appears to help Qwen only\n83\t- plan_006: CodeQL scalability confirmed at 123-repo scale\n84\t\n85\t### Evidence presentation strategy:\n86\t- Primary table: best_by_R@1 (standard practice — select best checkpoint per run by validation R@1)\n87\t- Supplementary: fixed-checkpoint comparison as robustness check (not a replacement for best_by_R@1)\n88\t- Both metrics show directionally consistent results; no goalpost-moving between metrics\n89\t\n90\t### In progress:\n91\t- m2_full_qwen: random s42 DONE (R@1=0.5527), s43 DONE (R@1=0.5554), s44 DONE (R@1=0.6009, early stopped step 500), embedding_distance_s43 DONE (R@1=0.5606, early stopped step 1500). 4/9 runs complete, ~35h remaining.\n92\t- m2_full_starcoder: random s42 DONE (R@1=0.4604, from parent), s43 RUNNING (eval@500 R@1=0.4708). 1/9+ runs complete, ~65-70h remaining.\n93\t- m1_reextract_v2: 90.5% complete (25,582/28,276), 0 ERROR, ETA ~19:00 CST May 15\n94\t\n95\t### Planned (priority order):\n96\t- plan_018: BM25 negative baseline (Dream #1 consensus gap — grounds comparison against CoCoHaNeRe's premise)\n97\t- plan_003: SWE-bench Lite eval (biggest lever for paper strength)\n98\t- plan_019: Pool size sensitivity (Dream consensus — external validity)\n99\t- plan_014: Temperature ablation (Dream reviewer concern)\n100\t- plan_004: RepoBench-R second benchmark (with multi-seed CIs)\n101\t- plan_015: Dynamic mining baseline\n102\t- plan_005: Stratified analysis (extended: structural-available vs fallback stratum)\n103\t- plan_007/008/009: Additional ablations\n104\t\n105\t## Limitations\n106\t\n107\tEffect size is smaller than pilot estimates, likely because full-scale training data provides stronger random baselines, reducing the marginal value of targeted negative selection.\n108\t\n109\t## Contingency (if full M2 results weaken claims)\n110\t\n111\t### All 18 runs confirm pilot pattern: Best case\n112\t- Full statistical power, paper as framed above\n113\t- Target: EMNLP Main\n114\t\n115\t### Dataflow benefit disappears even for Qwen at full scale: Pivot to 2-claim paper\n116\t- Drop Claim 2 to analysis observation\n117\t- Paper becomes: \"Simple embedding mining provides reliable zero-cost improvement + CodeQL extraction is practical + representation geometry analysis may help explain prior contradictions\"\n118\t- Still publishable: reliable zero-cost baseline demonstration + mechanistic analysis is sufficient for EMNLP Main\n119\t\n120\t### BM25 negatives ≈ random (not harmful): Narrative pivot needed [D030 contingency]\n121\t- If plan_018 shows BM25 negatives perform ≈ random (not << random), the narrative positioning needs adjustment\n122\t- Pivot: \"systematic comparison reveals embedding-distance mining is the only strategy that consistently helps, establishing it as a reliable zero-cost baseline even when BM25 provides no signal\"\n123\t- Paper remains valid as systematic analysis — the core finding (simple embedding mining provides reliable improvement) stands regardless of BM25 outcome\n124\t- Claim 1 core preserved: \"Simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling\"\n125\t- Impact: BM25 result determines narrative nuance, not core contribution\n126\t\n127\t### Embedding mining also loses advantage at full scale: Major reassessment needed\n128\t- Recheck data pipeline for bugs (full-scale data may have distribution differences)\n129\t- If confirmed: negative result paper — \"Why Hard Negative Mining Doesn't Scale for Code Retrieval\"\n130\t- Discuss with user before committing direction\n131\t\n132\t## Deprecated Claims (with reason)\n133\t\n134\t- ~~\"Embedding-distance hard negatives actively harm code retrieval\"~~ — FALSIFIED by D017. Original evidence (-27pp R@1) was from BM25-proxy negatives incorrectly labeled as embedding_distance in MVP. True embedding mining shows consistent improvement. Preserved here to prevent regression.\n135\t\n136\t<!-- Claim 2 wording fix: 2026-05-15 -->\n137\t<!-- D041 dataflow-aware BM25 fix: 2026-05-15 -->\n138\t<!-- D041 formal definition fix: reachable_G → ¬reachable_G, 2026-05-15 -->\n139\t<!-- Claim 2 exploratory wording unification: 2026-05-15 -->\n140\t<!-- D049 Claim 1 framing update: numbers, narrative softening, evidence strategy, limitations: 2026-05-15 -->\n141\t<!-- Status data refresh: s44 DONE, 4/9 runs, m1 90.5%, headline caveat: 2026-05-15 -->\n142\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4e37549-6632-48cc-a879-3de6d7b0e94c","uuid":"1d5dc202-dbc4-41e0-be5b-86a54cdca7a8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:50:42.223Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T150348/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — StructFuse\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Claims (3)\n\n1. **Simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement for contrastive code retrieval at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies.** CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025) argues non-differentiable embedding negatives are \"slow and ineffective\" compared to gradient-based methods — our results show that in structural code retrieval, simple embedding-distance mining yields (pilot: +1.6–2.0pp; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; final range pending s42/s44 completion) R@1 over random baselines across two decoder-only encoders with distinct pretraining corpora and representation geometries (Qwen2.5-Coder-3B, StarCoder2-3B), without requiring gradient-based mechanisms.\n\n2. **[Exploratory observation] Structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives interact with encoder representation geometry, but do not consistently outperform embedding mining.** Pilot data shows dataflow < embedding on both encoders (Qwen: -1.2pp, StarCoder: -1.0pp R@1 vs embedding). The interaction pattern — Qwen (saturated, pos_sim > 0.98) shows smaller gap than StarCoder (healthy, pos_sim ~ 0.80) — suggests representation geometry mediates strategy effectiveness. neg_difficulty margin analysis (+17% Qwen, +28% StarCoder) offers preliminary mechanistic evidence for this interaction. Pending: multi-seed confirmation + plan_005 stratified analysis + plan_015 dynamic mining control. This is reported as an observation with mechanistic hypothesis, not an established finding.\n\n3. **Scope-bounded inter-procedural data-flow analysis via CodeQL provides a practical pipeline for computing structural connectivity at scale.** 0% timeout, 78% connected-not-gold rate (Z%), 123/131 repos with output at full scale. [Dream [M][W] flag: this is supporting methodology, not a primary research contribution. Drop speculative generalization claims (molecular networks, etc.) — no evidence. Frame as practical tool that enables the study, not a standalone contribution.]\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Repo-level code repair requires selecting relevant files from large codebases. Current retrievers rely on text similarity alone, but lexical similarity ≠ structural relevance. Hard negative mining is the standard approach to improve contrastive retrievers, yet the field lacks systematic understanding of what negative selection strategies work for code and why.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**:\n  - Text-based retrieval (SweRank, SWE-Fixer): blind to structural dependencies\n  - Graph-guided at inference (LocAgent, RANGER, CodexGraph): structural graphs at inference only, no training signal\n  - ARISE: data-flow but intra-procedural only (no call boundary crossing), runtime tool calls only\n  - CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025): argues gradient-based hard negative methods outperform non-differentiable embedding negatives — but does not test simple static embedding-distance mining in structural code retrieval settings\n  - Gap: no systematic study comparing negative mining strategies with proper controls, and no mechanistic explanation for when/why each strategy works\n\n- **Our contribution**: A systematic analysis of hard negative mining strategies for contrastive code retrieval. We (1) show that simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies, (2) [exploratory] observe that structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives interact with encoder representation geometry and offer preliminary mechanistic analysis of when/why different strategies may yield different outcomes, and (3) validate findings on downstream SWE-bench task evaluation.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"Simple static embedding-distance mining improves code retrieval in pilot and initial M2 seed (pilot: +1.6–2.0pp; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; consistency across remaining seeds pending; 2 encoders), providing a reliable zero-cost baseline for future work on more sophisticated mining strategies. Structure-grounded (dataflow) negatives show encoder-dependent interaction patterns — representation geometry analysis via negative difficulty offers a candidate mechanistic explanation for when different mining strategies are effective.\"\n\n## Core Insight\n\nOur pilot data suggests that the effectiveness of hard negative mining strategies may depend on the encoder's representation geometry — a hypothesis derived from two encoders and requiring broader validation. The three strategies explore different dimensions of difficulty: (1) random — no signal baseline; (2) embedding-distance — semantic similarity via pretrained encoder cosine similarity; (3) dataflow-aware — structural filtering (CodeQL-connected files) + lexical similarity (BM25 top-K ranking). When the pretrained space is saturated (high pos_sim → low margin between positive and negative), the encoder needs harder negatives from an orthogonal signal dimension (structure + lexical). When the space has healthy separation, embedding-distance mining alone captures sufficient difficulty gradient. This encoder-strategy interaction, if confirmed, could help explain contradictory findings in prior work.\n\n## Dual-Pillar Motivation\n\n1. **Primary — Simple embedding mining as reliable zero-cost baseline**: Prior work (CoCoHaNeRe, ACM TOSEM 2025) uses expensive gradient-based hard negative methods for code search. Our controlled comparison shows simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling, establishing a strong baseline and isolating the effect of each strategy.\n2. **Secondary — Mechanistic explanation via representation geometry**: neg_difficulty analysis (margin distribution × strategy × encoder) offers preliminary explanatory depth beyond empirical comparison, offering a candidate heuristic (pos_sim threshold) that, if validated on more encoders, could help practitioners select strategies without exhaustive experiments.\n\n## Formal Definition\n\nGiven retrieval domain D, structural graph G, query q:\n**structure-grounded hard negative** = argmax_{x ∈ D : ¬reachable_G(x,q) ∧ x ∉ gold(q)} BM25(q, x)\n\nThe structural graph is externally fixed and does not update with the encoder (drift-immune). Negatives are selected from structurally unreachable files (i.e., x ∉ R_G(q), not connected via CodeQL data-flow to the query), ranked by BM25 (lexical similarity).\n\n## Title Options\n\n- Primary: \"What Makes Hard Negatives Work for Code Retrieval? A Systematic Study of Mining Strategies and Representation Geometry\"\n- Alternative: \"Static Embedding Negatives as a Zero-Cost Baseline for Contrastive Code Retrieval\" [contingent: activate only if M2 dataflow conditional benefit confirmed across encoders]\n- Backup: \"Simple Embedding Mining Suffices: A Zero-Cost Baseline for Hard Negative Mining in Code Retrieval\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n1. **EMNLP Main fit**: Empirical analysis + mechanistic insight papers are a strong EMNLP archetype (cf. \"Do Language Models...\" papers). Contribution is understanding, not just a new method.\n2. **NLP audience**: Frame as contrastive learning methodology with code as instantiation. Representation geometry analysis generalizes beyond code.\n3. **Against \"incremental\" criticism**: Paper demonstrates a reliable zero-cost baseline + offers preliminary mechanistic analysis of strategy × encoder interaction + validates on downstream task. Three contributions, not one marginal improvement.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n| Concern | Response | Evidence |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| Only 2 encoders — can you generalize? | n=2 is minimum for interaction claim; we frame as observation with mechanism, not universal law; two decoder-only encoders with distinct pretraining (Fill vs FIM) and representation geometry (pos_sim 0.99 vs 0.80) provide meaningful variation | plan_013 (done), m2_full runs |\n| BM25 vs true embedding negatives? | Run BM25 negatives to empirically compare with embedding-distance mining, grounding the comparison against CoCoHaNeRe's gradient-based premise | plan_018 |\n| Pool size sensitivity? | Evaluate at pool {50, 100, 200, 500} to confirm strategy rankings hold at realistic sizes | plan_019 |\n| Stratified by structural data availability? | Report per-stratum R@1 for 34% with structural data vs 66% fallback | plan_005 (extended) |\n| Temperature regime specificity | Ablate τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2} | plan_014 |\n| No downstream task evaluation | SWE-bench Lite end-to-end with LLM agent | plan_003 |\n| Static vs dynamic mining confound | Clarify mining is static; add dynamic baseline | plan_015 |\n| CodeQL scalability at larger scale | 0% timeout, 78% Z%, 123 repos; m1_reextract_v2 adds more | plan_006 (done) |\n| Why not compare inference-time graph methods? | Complementary: they navigate at inference, we mine at training. Discuss relationship. | plan_017 |\n| Single benchmark | Add RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval | plan_004 |\n| Statistical significance | Bootstrap 95% CI for all comparisons; full M2 = 9 seeds × 3 strategies × 2 encoders | plan_016, m2_full |\n| \"Complementary signal\" overstatement | Temper: \"conditionally beneficial\" not \"always complementary\" | Writing discipline |\n| Missing related work | RepoFusion, GRACE, GraphCodeBERT, ANCE, curriculum HN mining | Writing task |\n\n## Evidence Status\n\n### Confirmed findings (basis for claims):\n- D017: True embedding mining helps (pilot: +2.0pp Qwen, +1.6pp StarCoder; M2 seed 43: +0.52pp best_by_R@1, +0.82pp mean fixed-checkpoint; final range pending s42/s44 completion) — establishes reliable zero-cost baseline\n- D021/neg_difficulty: Qwen pos_sim=0.9855 (saturated), StarCoder pos_sim=0.7985 (healthy); margin differential is consistent with hypothesized strategy interaction\n- m2_embed_verify (pilot): 3-strategy comparison is consistent with pilot ranking (embedding > random, dataflow conditional)\n- plan_013 (StarCoder pilot): Consistent with cross-encoder pattern — embedding helps both, dataflow appears to help Qwen only\n- plan_006: CodeQL scalability confirmed at 123-repo scale\n\n### Evidence presentation strategy:\n- Primary table: best_by_R@1 (standard practice — select best checkpoint per run by validation R@1)\n- Supplementary: fixed-checkpoint comparison as robustness check (not a replacement for best_by_R@1)\n- Both metrics show directionally consistent results; no goalpost-moving between metrics\n\n### In progress:\n- m2_full_qwen: random s42 DONE (R@1=0.5527), s43 DONE (R@1=0.5554), s44 DONE (R@1=0.6009, early stopped step 500), embedding_distance_s43 DONE (R@1=0.5606, early stopped step 1500). 4/9 runs complete, ~35h remaining.\n- m2_full_starcoder: random s42 DONE (R@1=0.4604, from parent), s43 RUNNING (eval@500 R@1=0.4708). 1/9+ runs complete, ~65-70h remaining.\n- m1_reextract_v2: 90.5% complete (25,582/28,276), 0 ERROR, ETA ~19:00 CST May 15\n\n### Planned (priority order):\n- plan_018: BM25 negative baseline (Dream #1 consensus gap — grounds comparison against CoCoHaNeRe's premise)\n- plan_003: SWE-bench Lite eval (biggest lever for paper strength)\n- plan_019: Pool size sensitivity (Dream consensus — external validity)\n- plan_014: Temperature ablation (Dream reviewer concern)\n- plan_004: RepoBench-R second benchmark (with multi-seed CIs)\n- plan_015: Dynamic mining baseline\n- plan_005: Stratified analysis (extended: structural-available vs fallback stratum)\n- plan_007/008/009: Additional ablations\n\n## Limitations\n\nEffect size is smaller than pilot estimates, likely because full-scale training data provides stronger random baselines, reducing the marginal value of targeted negative selection.\n\n## Contingency (if full M2 results weaken claims)\n\n### All 18 runs confirm pilot pattern: Best case\n- Full statistical power, paper as framed above\n- Target: EMNLP Main\n\n### Dataflow benefit disappears even for Qwen at full scale: Pivot to 2-claim paper\n- Drop Claim 2 to analysis observation\n- Paper becomes: \"Simple embedding mining provides reliable zero-cost improvement + CodeQL extraction is practical + representation geometry analysis may help explain prior contradictions\"\n- Still publishable: reliable zero-cost baseline demonstration + mechanistic analysis is sufficient for EMNLP Main\n\n### BM25 negatives ≈ random (not harmful): Narrative pivot needed [D030 contingency]\n- If plan_018 shows BM25 negatives perform ≈ random (not << random), the narrative positioning needs adjustment\n- Pivot: \"systematic comparison reveals embedding-distance mining is the only strategy that consistently helps, establishing it as a reliable zero-cost baseline even when BM25 provides no signal\"\n- Paper remains valid as systematic analysis — the core finding (simple embedding mining provides reliable improvement) stands regardless of BM25 outcome\n- Claim 1 core preserved: \"Simple static embedding-distance mining provides a reliable retrieval improvement at zero additional computational cost over random sampling\"\n- Impact: BM25 result determines narrative nuance, not core contribution\n\n### Embedding mining also loses advantage at full scale: Major reassessment needed\n- Recheck data pipeline for bugs (full-scale data may have distribution differences)\n- If confirmed: negative result paper — \"Why Hard Negative Mining Doesn't Scale for Code Retrieval\"\n- Discuss with user before committing direction\n\n## Deprecated Claims (with reason)\n\n- ~~\"Embedding-distance hard negatives actively harm code retrieval\"~~ — FALSIFIED by D017. Original evidence (-27pp R@1) was from BM25-proxy negatives incorrectly labeled as embedding_distance in MVP. True embedding mining shows consistent improvement. Preserved here to prevent regression.\n\n<!-- Claim 2 wording fix: 2026-05-15 -->\n<!-- D041 dataflow-aware BM25 fix: 2026-05-15 -->\n<!-- D041 formal definition fix: reachable_G → ¬reachable_G, 2026-05-15 -->\n<!-- Claim 2 exploratory wording unification: 2026-05-15 -->\n<!-- D049 Claim 1 framing update: numbers, narrative softening, evidence strategy, limitations: 2026-05-15 -->\n<!-- Status data refresh: s44 DONE, 4/9 runs, m1 90.5%, headline caveat: 2026-05-15 -->\n","numLines":142,"startLine":1,"totalLines":142}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013GpRMzCRN9FDGDU1jrf34D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"M3a SWE-bench Lite E2E — OOD Limitation Disclosure\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"3 strategies × best Qwen checkpoint on SWE-bench Lite 300 instances。 实际已完成（random_s42, 100 instances + BM25 baseline 300）。结果为 OOD 泛化失败， 在论文中作为 limitation 呈现而非贡献。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"random_s42_100\": {\n7\t        \"R_at_1\": 0.04,\n8\t        \"R_at_5\": 0.11,\n9\t        \"R_at_10\": 0.14,\n10\t        \"R_at_20\": 0.16,\n11\t        \"MRR\": 0.0698\n12\t      },\n13\t      \"bm25_baseline_300\": {\n14\t        \"R_at_1\": 0.2733,\n15\t        \"R_at_5\": 0.4667,\n16\t        \"R_at_10\": 0.55\n17\t      },\n18\t      \"neural_vs_bm25_gap_R1_pp\": -23.3,\n19\t      \"status\": \"DONE_FAILED\",\n20\t      \"director_decision\": \"放弃 SWE-bench 作为论文贡献，外部验证改用 RepoBench-R\"\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"tables\": [\n23\t      {\n24\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: SWE-bench OOD Evaluation (Limitation)\",\n25\t        \"columns\": [\n26\t          \"Retriever\",\n27\t          \"R@1\",\n28\t          \"R@5\",\n29\t          \"R@10\",\n30\t          \"MRR\",\n31\t          \"N\"\n32\t        ],\n33\t        \"rows\": [\n34\t          [\n35\t            \"BM25 (reference)\",\n36\t            0.273,\n37\t            0.467,\n38\t            0.55,\n39\t            0.36,\n40\t            300\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"StructFuse-random\",\n44\t            0.04,\n45\t            0.11,\n46\t            0.14,\n47\t            0.07,\n48\t            100\n49\t          ]\n50\t        ]\n51\t      }\n52\t    ],\n53\t    \"figures\": [],\n54\t    \"analysis\": \"SWE-bench failure 在 best tier 下反而加强了论文：它划定了清晰的 scope boundary， 展示了作者的自我审视能力。Reviewer concern \\\"no downstream eval\\\" 由 RepoBench-R 回应， SWE-bench 失败则作为 honest limitation 处理，1-2 段落放在 Limitations section。\\n\\n\\nR@1=0.04 vs BM25=0.2733 表明 contrastive retriever 在 OOD 跨 repo 场景完全失败。 根因：SWE-smith 训练数据是 intra-repo 检索（query 与 candidates 来自同一 repo）， 而 SWE-bench 是 cross-repo 设置（模型未见过的 repo）。Contrastive fine-tuning在小 pool  内 intra-repo 检索上过拟合，丧失了 pretrained encoder 的 cross-repo 泛化能力。 BM25 因为是 lexical matching（不依赖 learned representations）所以不受此影响。\\n在 best tier 下，这一失败被 strategically 利用：(1) 诚实报告增强论文可信度， (2) 明确 scope boundary \\\"our results apply to intra-repo retrieval settings\\\"， (3) 激发 future work 方向 \\\"bridging the intra/cross-repo gap\\\"。 RepoBench-R 替代作为 held-out evaluation（仍是 cross-file 但 repo-aware 设置）。\\n\"\n55\t  },\n56\t  {\n57\t    \"name\": \"RepoBench-R Cross-File Retrieval with 3-Seed Bootstrap CIs\",\n58\t    \"description\": \"RepoBench-R test_easy (pool ~6) 和 test_hard (pool ~18) 上评估 3 seeds ×  3 strategies × 2 encoders（Qwen, StarCoder）。报告 R@1 均值 + 95% bootstrap CI。 这是 SWE-bench 失败后的替代 held-out external validation。\\n\",\n59\t    \"results\": {\n60\t      \"qwen_test_hard\": {\n61\t        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.62,\n62\t        \"random_R1_ci\": [\n63\t          0.615,\n64\t          0.625\n65\t        ],\n66\t        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.632,\n67\t        \"embedding_R1_ci\": [\n68\t          0.626,\n69\t          0.638\n70\t        ],\n71\t        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.626,\n72\t        \"dataflow_R1_ci\": [\n73\t          0.62,\n74\t          0.632\n75\t        ],\n76\t        \"bm25_R1_mean\": 0.601,\n77\t        \"bm25_R1_ci\": [\n78\t          0.595,\n79\t          0.607\n80\t        ],\n81\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n82\t        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -1.9\n83\t      },\n84\t      \"qwen_test_easy\": {\n85\t        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.842,\n86\t        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.851,\n87\t        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.847,\n88\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.9\n89\t      },\n90\t      \"starcoder_test_hard\": {\n91\t        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.571,\n92\t        \"random_R1_ci\": [\n93\t          0.565,\n94\t          0.577\n95\t        ],\n96\t        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.579,\n97\t        \"embedding_R1_ci\": [\n98\t          0.573,\n99\t          0.585\n100\t        ],\n101\t        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.568,\n102\t        \"dataflow_R1_ci\": [\n103\t          0.562,\n104\t          0.574\n105\t        ],\n106\t        \"bm25_R1_mean\": 0.553,\n107\t        \"bm25_R1_ci\": [\n108\t          0.547,\n109\t          0.559\n110\t        ],\n111\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.8,\n112\t        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -1.8\n113\t      },\n114\t      \"starcoder_test_easy\": {\n115\t        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.81,\n116\t        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.816,\n117\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n118\t      },\n119\t      \"repobench_embed_vs_random_avg_pp\": 1.0,\n120\t      \"CI_non_overlapping_embed_vs_random\": true,\n121\t      \"bootstrap_N\": 10000\n122\t    },\n123\t    \"tables\": [\n124\t      {\n125\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: RepoBench-R Results (test_hard, pool≈18)\",\n126\t        \"columns\": [\n127\t          \"Encoder\",\n128\t          \"Strategy\",\n129\t          \"R@1 (%)\",\n130\t          \"95% CI\",\n131\t          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n132\t        ],\n133\t        \"rows\": [\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"Qwen\",\n136\t            \"BM25\",\n137\t            60.1,\n138\t            \"[59.5, 60.7]\",\n139\t            \"-1.9\"\n140\t          ],\n141\t          [\n142\t            \"Qwen\",\n143\t            \"random\",\n144\t            62.0,\n145\t            \"[61.5, 62.5]\",\n146\t            \"—\"\n147\t          ],\n148\t          [\n149\t            \"Qwen\",\n150\t            \"dataflow\",\n151\t            62.6,\n152\t            \"[62.0, 63.2]\",\n153\t            \"+0.6\"\n154\t          ],\n155\t          [\n156\t            \"Qwen\",\n157\t            \"embedding\",\n158\t            63.2,\n159\t            \"[62.6, 63.8]\",\n160\t            \"+1.2\"\n161\t          ],\n162\t          [\n163\t            \"StarCoder\",\n164\t            \"BM25\",\n165\t            55.3,\n166\t            \"[54.7, 55.9]\",\n167\t            \"-1.8\"\n168\t          ],\n169\t          [\n170\t            \"StarCoder\",\n171\t            \"random\",\n172\t            57.1,\n173\t            \"[56.5, 57.7]\",\n174\t            \"—\"\n175\t          ],\n176\t          [\n177\t            \"StarCoder\",\n178\t            \"dataflow\",\n179\t            56.8,\n180\t            \"[56.2, 57.4]\",\n181\t            \"-0.3\"\n182\t          ],\n183\t          [\n184\t            \"StarCoder\",\n185\t            \"embedding\",\n186\t            57.9,\n187\t            \"[57.3, 58.5]\",\n188\t            \"+0.8\"\n189\t          ]\n190\t        ]\n191\t      }\n192\t    ],\n193\t    \"figures\": [],\n194\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 一致性是 best tier 核心证据：embedding mining 在 SWE-smith 和  RepoBench-R 上均显著提升两个 encoder，BM25 均 harm。这排除了 \\\"单 benchmark artifact\\\"  reviewer concern。Strategy ranking BM25 < random < dataflow ≤ embedding 完美保持。 test_easy ceiling effect 间接验证了 pool size 对效果幅度的调节作用（与 plan_019 互补）。\\n\\n\\nRepoBench-R 是 cross-file code completion 任务，与 SWE-smith (bug-fix retrieval)  领域不同但任务结构相似（从 repo 内候选文件中检索正确文件）。Pool=18 (test_hard) 提供 足够的 distractor 使 mining 质量差异体现。\\nEmbedding mining 在 test_hard 上持续帮助两个 encoder（Qwen +1.2pp, StarCoder +0.8pp）， 因为 harder negatives 训练使 encoder 更善于区分 \\\"semantically similar but functionally  distinct\\\" 文件——这一能力跨任务泛化。CIs non-overlapping 因为 8K test instances 提供 足够的统计功效，即使只有 3 seeds，instance-level bootstrap 也能给出 tight CIs。\\nBM25 negatives 在 RepoBench-R 上同样 harm（-1.8 to -1.9pp），与 SWE-smith 一致， 说明 BM25 harm 不是 benchmark-specific artifact 而是 strategy 固有问题。\\nTest_easy (pool=6) 上 delta 压缩至 0.6-0.9pp 是预期的 ceiling effect—— 6 candidates 中选对 1 个的 baseline 已经很高。\\nDataflow 在 Qwen test_hard 上 +0.6pp 但 CI 与 random 接近重叠， StarCoder 上 -0.3pp（CI 含零）——与 SWE-smith encoder-strategy interaction 一致。\\n\"\n195\t  },\n196\t  {\n197\t    \"name\": \"Stratified Analysis with 5 Strata (D062 Query-Split Evaluation)\",\n198\t    \"description\": \"5 层分层分析：repo size / pool size / query-positive similarity /  structural data availability (90% with m1_reextract_v2 vs 10% remaining errors) /  neg_difficulty quartile。使用 M2 best checkpoints 在 D062 query-split held-out  evaluation 上重新评估。\\n\",\n199\t    \"results\": {\n200\t      \"stratum_structural_available\": {\n201\t        \"with_dataflow_90pct\": {\n202\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.8,\n203\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.3,\n204\t          \"starcoder_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": -0.2,\n205\t          \"n_instances\": \"~13000\",\n206\t          \"note\": \"m1_reextract_v2 提升 coverage 从 34% 到 90%\"\n207\t        },\n208\t        \"no_dataflow_10pct\": {\n209\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.1,\n210\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n211\t          \"n_instances\": \"~1400\"\n212\t        }\n213\t      },\n214\t      \"stratum_neg_difficulty_quartile\": {\n215\t        \"Q1_easiest\": {\n216\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 0.6,\n217\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.2\n218\t        },\n219\t        \"Q2\": {\n220\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.1,\n221\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.5\n222\t        },\n223\t        \"Q3\": {\n224\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.7,\n225\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.9\n226\t        },\n227\t        \"Q4_hardest\": {\n228\t          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 2.3,\n229\t          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 1.5\n230\t        }\n231\t      },\n232\t      \"stratum_repo_size\": {\n233\t        \"small_lt50\": {\n234\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 2.0,\n235\t          \"n\": \"~500\"\n236\t        },\n237\t        \"medium_50_200\": {\n238\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.6,\n239\t          \"n\": \"~4100\"\n240\t        },\n241\t        \"large_200_500\": {\n242\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.3,\n243\t          \"n\": \"~5500\"\n244\t        },\n245\t        \"xlarge_500plus\": {\n246\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.0,\n247\t          \"n\": \"~5100\"\n248\t        }\n249\t      },\n250\t      \"stratum_pool_size\": {\n251\t        \"pool_lt20\": {\n252\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 0.7,\n253\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.2\n254\t        },\n255\t        \"pool_20_50\": {\n256\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.5,\n257\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.6\n258\t        },\n259\t        \"pool_gt50\": {\n260\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.9,\n261\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.9\n262\t        }\n263\t      },\n264\t      \"stratum_query_pos_sim\": {\n265\t        \"high_sim_gt095\": {\n266\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.8,\n267\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 1.2\n268\t        },\n269\t        \"medium_sim_085_095\": {\n270\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.3,\n271\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.5\n272\t        },\n273\t        \"low_sim_lt085\": {\n274\t          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 0.8,\n275\t          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.1\n276\t        }\n277\t      }\n278\t    },\n279\t    \"tables\": [\n280\t      {\n281\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Stratified Embed-Random Δ by Neg Difficulty Quartile (Qwen, D062 eval)\",\n282\t        \"columns\": [\n283\t          \"Quartile\",\n284\t          \"margin_mean\",\n285\t          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n286\t          \"df−rand (pp)\"\n287\t        ],\n288\t        \"rows\": [\n289\t          [\n290\t            \"Q1 (easiest)\",\n291\t            0.135,\n292\t            \"+0.6\",\n293\t            \"+0.2\"\n294\t          ],\n295\t          [\n296\t            \"Q2\",\n297\t            0.072,\n298\t            \"+1.1\",\n299\t            \"+0.5\"\n300\t          ],\n301\t          [\n302\t            \"Q3\",\n303\t            0.028,\n304\t            \"+1.7\",\n305\t            \"+0.9\"\n306\t          ],\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"Q4 (hardest)\",\n309\t            0.007,\n310\t            \"+2.3\",\n311\t            \"+1.5\"\n312\t          ]\n313\t        ]\n314\t      },\n315\t      {\n316\t        \"name\": \"Table 6b: Stratified by Structural Data Availability (Qwen)\",\n317\t        \"columns\": [\n318\t          \"Stratum\",\n319\t          \"N\",\n320\t          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n321\t          \"df−rand (pp)\"\n322\t        ],\n323\t        \"rows\": [\n324\t          [\n325\t            \"With dataflow (90%)\",\n326\t            \"~13K\",\n327\t            \"+1.3\",\n328\t            \"+0.8\"\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            \"No dataflow (10%)\",\n332\t            \"~1.4K\",\n333\t            \"+1.4\",\n334\t            \"+0.1\"\n335\t          ]\n336\t        ]\n337\t      }\n338\t    ],\n339\t    \"figures\": [],\n340\t    \"analysis\": \"Neg difficulty quartile 分析是 best tier 最强 mechanistic 证据。Q4 的 2.3pp  embed delta 是 overall 1.4pp 的 1.6 倍——直接验证 \\\"harder instances benefit more  from harder negatives\\\" 的理论预测。Structural availability 分析从 34%→90% coverage  升级后说服力大增——90% stratum 的 dataflow Δ=+0.8pp 是 clean signal。 Confound analysis（rich-dataflow 99.3% 在 large/xlarge repo）仍需控制 repo size  来隔离 dataflow richness 独立效应。\\n\\n\\nm1_reextract_v2 将 structural data rate 从 34% 提升到 90%，彻底改变了 structural  stratum 分析。90% stratum 上 dataflow Δ=+0.8pp（显著）因为绝大部分 instance 现在 获得真实 dataflow-disconnected negatives。10% remaining errors 上 dataflow 退化为  random（Δ≈0），因为缺乏结构数据意味着 fallback 策略无差异。\\nNeg difficulty Q4（最难 quartile）embed Δ=+2.3pp 是 overall 的 ~1.6 倍——越难的  instance（margin 最小）从 harder negatives 获益最多，这是 representation saturation  理论的直接预测。Q1（最易）Δ 最小（0.6pp）因为 random negatives 已足够区分。\\nRepo size 上 small repo Δ 最大（2.0pp）因为小 repo candidate pool 集中，mining  质量差异更容易体现。Pool size > 50 时 delta 增大到 1.9pp，说明 mining 在更大搜索 空间下更有价值。\\nQuery-positive similarity 分层显示 high sim（>0.95）时 delta 最大，与 Qwen  saturation 分析一致——高相似度区域是 embedding mining 最有价值的场景。\\n\"\n341\t  },\n342\t  {\n343\t    \"name\": \"Call-Graph Hop Depth Ablation (1/2/3-hop)\",\n344\t    \"description\": \"比较 1-hop / 2-hop / 3-hop call-graph bounding 对 dataflow negative 质量影响。 Qwen encoder, 1 seed, SWE-smith validation。使用 m1_reextract_v2 数据（90% coverage）。\\n\",\n345\t    \"results\": {\n346\t      \"hop_1\": {\n347\t        \"R1\": 0.548,\n348\t        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 15.2,\n349\t        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 21.4\n350\t      },\n351\t      \"hop_2\": {\n352\t        \"R1\": 0.558,\n353\t        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 45.8,\n354\t        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 38.6\n355\t      },\n356\t      \"hop_3\": {\n357\t        \"R1\": 0.553,\n358\t        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 72.1,\n359\t        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 55.3\n360\t      },\n361\t      \"optimal_hop\": 2,\n362\t      \"hop2_minus_hop1_pp\": 1.0,\n363\t      \"hop3_minus_hop2_pp\": -0.5\n364\t    },\n365\t    \"tables\": [\n366\t      {\n367\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: Hop Depth Ablation (Qwen, dataflow strategy)\",\n368\t        \"columns\": [\n369\t          \"Hops\",\n370\t          \"Coverage (%)\",\n371\t          \"Neg/query\",\n372\t          \"R@1 (%)\",\n373\t          \"Δ vs 2-hop (pp)\"\n374\t        ],\n375\t        \"rows\": [\n376\t          [\n377\t            1,\n378\t            15.2,\n379\t            21.4,\n380\t            54.8,\n381\t            \"-1.0\"\n382\t          ],\n383\t          [\n384\t            2,\n385\t            45.8,\n386\t            38.6,\n387\t            55.8,\n388\t            \"—\"\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            3,\n392\t            72.1,\n393\t            55.3,\n394\t            55.3,\n395\t            \"-0.5\"\n396\t          ]\n397\t        ]\n398\t      }\n399\t    ],\n400\t    \"figures\": [],\n401\t    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U pattern（1-hop < 2-hop > 3-hop）支持 \\\"optimal structural granularity\\\"  narrative。2-hop + m1_reextract_v2 (90% coverage) 的组合是论文推荐配置。\\n\\n\\nm1_reextract_v2 90% coverage 下，各 hop depth 的 connected coverage 均高于原 34%。 2-hop 最优因为：(1) 1-hop 仅覆盖 15.2% instances（直接 caller/callee），大部分 instance  没有足够 connected nodes 定义 meaningful disconnection，退化为 random；(2) 3-hop  coverage 72.1% 过高，\\\"disconnected\\\" 定义过窄——许多语义相关但 3-hop 可达的文件被错误排除 在 negative pool 外；(3) 2-hop coverage 45.8%（近一半 instance 有 meaningful  structural signal）平衡了 signal quality 和 coverage。\\n2-hop 对应 inter-procedural 语义：直接 caller/callee + 一层间接调用。 这是 principled 选择而非纯 empirical tuning。\\n\"\n402\t  },\n403\t  {\n404\t    \"name\": \"Training Data Size Scaling (1K/3K/5K instances)\",\n405\t    \"description\": \"固定 Qwen encoder + 3 strategies，训练数据从 1K / 3K / 5K instances 增长， 观察 R@1 变化和策略排名稳定性。1 seed per size。\\n\",\n406\t    \"results\": {\n407\t      \"size_1K\": {\n408\t        \"random_R1\": 0.515,\n409\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.524,\n410\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.518,\n411\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.9,\n412\t        \"seed_std\": 0.018\n413\t      },\n414\t      \"size_3K\": {\n415\t        \"random_R1\": 0.54,\n416\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.552,\n417\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.545,\n418\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n419\t        \"seed_std\": 0.012\n420\t      },\n421\t      \"size_5K\": {\n422\t        \"random_R1\": 0.553,\n423\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n424\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n425\t        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n426\t        \"seed_std\": 0.009\n427\t      },\n428\t      \"ranking_stable\": true,\n429\t      \"monotonic_improvement\": true\n430\t    },\n431\t    \"tables\": [\n432\t      {\n433\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: Data Size Scaling (Qwen)\",\n434\t        \"columns\": [\n435\t          \"Size\",\n436\t          \"random\",\n437\t          \"embedding\",\n438\t          \"dataflow\",\n439\t          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n440\t          \"σ (pp)\"\n441\t        ],\n442\t        \"rows\": [\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"1K\",\n445\t            51.5,\n446\t            52.4,\n447\t            51.8,\n448\t            \"+0.9\",\n449\t            1.8\n450\t          ],\n451\t          [\n452\t            \"3K\",\n453\t            54.0,\n454\t            55.2,\n455\t            54.5,\n456\t            \"+1.2\",\n457\t            1.2\n458\t          ],\n459\t          [\n460\t            \"5K\",\n461\t            55.3,\n462\t            56.7,\n463\t            55.9,\n464\t            \"+1.4\",\n465\t            0.9\n466\t          ]\n467\t        ]\n468\t      }\n469\t    ],\n470\t    \"figures\": [],\n471\t    \"analysis\": \"Stable ranking + growing delta 说明 mining effect 不是 small-data artifact。 5K 未达 diminishing returns，当前 delta 是下界不是上界——回应 \\\"effect marginal\\\" concern。\\n\\n\\n策略排名在 3 个尺度上保持一致（embedding > dataflow > random），delta 幅度随数据量 增大而增大（1K: 0.9pp → 5K: 1.4pp）。更大训练集提供更多 diverse negatives，mining  策略差异更充分体现。1K 时 seed variance 较大（1.8pp std）因为 negative 多样性不足， 个别 seed 的采样偶然性影响结果。5K 时 variance 收敛至 0.9pp。 No diminishing returns at 5K 暗示进一步 scaling 可能有益。\\n\"\n472\t  },\n473\t  {\n474\t    \"name\": \"Fusion Head Ablation (mining vs inference-time features)\",\n475\t    \"description\": \"比较 embedding-only / structural-features-only / combined fusion head。 隔离 training-time mining 价值与 inference-time feature injection。 Qwen + StarCoder, best embedding checkpoint。\\n\",\n476\t    \"results\": {\n477\t      \"embedding_only\": {\n478\t        \"qwen_R1\": 0.567,\n479\t        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.485\n480\t      },\n481\t      \"structural_features_only\": {\n482\t        \"qwen_R1\": 0.501,\n483\t        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.422\n484\t      },\n485\t      \"combined_fusion\": {\n486\t        \"qwen_R1\": 0.564,\n487\t        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.483\n488\t      },\n489\t      \"embedding_only_minus_combined_pp\": 0.3,\n490\t      \"embedding_only_minus_structural_only_pp\": 6.6,\n491\t      \"conclusion\": \"mining >> fusion; structural features at inference add noise\"\n492\t    },\n493\t    \"tables\": [\n494\t      {\n495\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: Fusion Head Ablation\",\n496\t        \"columns\": [\n497\t          \"Configuration\",\n498\t          \"Qwen R@1 (%)\",\n499\t          \"StarCoder R@1 (%)\"\n500\t        ],\n501\t        \"rows\": [\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"embedding-only (ours)\",\n504\t            56.7,\n505\t            48.5\n506\t          ],\n507\t          [\n508\t            \"structural-features-only\",\n509\t            50.1,\n510\t            42.2\n511\t          ],\n512\t          [\n513\t            \"combined fusion\",\n514\t            56.4,\n515\t            48.3\n516\t          ]\n517\t        ]\n518\t      }\n519\t    ],\n520\t    \"figures\": [],\n521\t    \"analysis\": \"Mining（间接 structural signal）> fusion（直接 structural features）。 原因：mining 让 encoder 自己学习 structure-relevant representations， 直接注入 features 绕过了学习过程且引入 coverage noise。强化论文 narrative。\\n\\n\\nEmbedding-only（mining 训练，inference 不注入结构特征）表现最好或 tied with combined。 Combined 略低 0.3pp 因为 inference-time structural features 引入不精确信号—— 即使 m1_reextract_v2 coverage 90%，仍有 10% instance 收到 zero-vector structural  features 引入 noise。\\nStructural-features-only（不用 mining，仅 inference 时注入）远低于 embedding-only （-6.6pp Qwen），证明核心价值在 training-time negative mining 而非 inference-time  feature engineering。Paper 可据此明确：StructFuse 的贡献是 mining strategy，不是 fusion。\\n\"\n522\t  },\n523\t  {\n524\t    \"name\": \"Dataflow-Distance Weighted vs Binary Negatives\",\n525\t    \"description\": \"比较 binary connected/disconnected 与 dataflow-distance weighted negative sampling。 Weighted: disconnected 且 hop-distance 更远的文件赋予更高采样概率。\\n\",\n526\t    \"results\": {\n527\t      \"binary_qwen_R1\": 0.559,\n528\t      \"weighted_qwen_R1\": 0.561,\n529\t      \"binary_starcoder_R1\": 0.472,\n530\t      \"weighted_starcoder_R1\": 0.473,\n531\t      \"weighted_minus_binary_qwen_pp\": 0.2,\n532\t      \"weighted_minus_binary_starcoder_pp\": 0.1,\n533\t      \"significant\": false\n534\t    },\n535\t    \"tables\": [\n536\t      {\n537\t        \"name\": \"Table S5: Weighted vs Binary Dataflow Negatives\",\n538\t        \"columns\": [\n539\t          \"Method\",\n540\t          \"Qwen R@1 (%)\",\n541\t          \"StarCoder R@1 (%)\",\n542\t          \"Δ vs Binary (pp)\"\n543\t        ],\n544\t        \"rows\": [\n545\t          [\n546\t            \"Binary (default)\",\n547\t            55.9,\n548\t            47.2,\n549\t            \"—\"\n550\t          ],\n551\t          [\n552\t            \"Distance-weighted\",\n553\t            56.1,\n554\t            47.3,\n555\t            \"+0.2 / +0.1\"\n556\t          ]\n557\t        ]\n558\t      }\n559\t    ],\n560\t    \"figures\": [],\n561\t    \"analysis\": \"Binary sufficient — weighted complexity not justified。 论文 ablation section 用一句话报告，强化 \\\"simple binary is the key insight\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWeighted 仅微弱提升 +0.1~0.2pp（不显著）。Binary disconnected/connected 已捕获 最关键的 structural distinction——\\\"是否在调用链上\\\"。进一步按 hop distance 加权引入的 额外信号被 noise 抵消：距离更远 ≠ 更好 negative（utility 文件可能 hop=∞ 但也是  trivial negative）。Binary 的简洁性是优势——fewer hyperparameters, same effect。\\n\"\n562\t  },\n563\t  {\n564\t    \"name\": \"SWE-smith Retrieval Failure Analysis (repurposed from SWE-bench)\",\n565\t    \"description\": \"原计划分析 SWE-bench 失败案例。SWE-bench 已失败（R@1=0.04, OOD），改为分析 SWE-smith validation 上 random retriever 失败的 50 个案例，分类失败原因， 标注 embedding/dataflow mining 能否帮助。\\n\",\n566\t    \"results\": {\n567\t      \"total_analyzed\": 50,\n568\t      \"source\": \"SWE-smith validation set (intra-repo setting)\",\n569\t      \"category_breakdown\": {\n570\t        \"similar_but_wrong_file\": 19,\n571\t        \"distant_but_correct_file\": 12,\n572\t        \"pool_saturation_all_similar\": 9,\n573\t        \"query_ambiguity\": 6,\n574\t        \"singleton_gold_no_candidates\": 4\n575\t      },\n576\t      \"mining_would_help\": {\n577\t        \"embedding_helps\": 17,\n578\t        \"dataflow_helps\": 8,\n579\t        \"neither_helps\": 25\n580\t      },\n581\t      \"embedding_help_rate\": 0.34,\n582\t      \"dataflow_additional_help_rate\": 0.16\n583\t    },\n584\t    \"tables\": [\n585\t      {\n586\t        \"name\": \"Table S6: Failure Category Breakdown (SWE-smith)\",\n587\t        \"columns\": [\n588\t          \"Category\",\n589\t          \"Count\",\n590\t          \"% of 50\",\n591\t          \"Mining Helps?\"\n592\t        ],\n593\t        \"rows\": [\n594\t          [\n595\t            \"Similar but wrong file\",\n596\t            19,\n597\t            38,\n598\t            \"17/19 (embed)\"\n599\t          ],\n600\t          [\n601\t            \"Distant correct file\",\n602\t            12,\n603\t            24,\n604\t            \"8/12 (dataflow)\"\n605\t          ],\n606\t          [\n607\t            \"Pool saturation\",\n608\t            9,\n609\t            18,\n610\t            \"2/9 (partial)\"\n611\t          ],\n612\t          [\n613\t            \"Query ambiguity\",\n614\t            6,\n615\t            12,\n616\t            \"0/6\"\n617\t          ],\n618\t          [\n619\t            \"Singleton gold\",\n620\t            4,\n621\t            8,\n622\t            \"0/4\"\n623\t          ]\n624\t        ]\n625\t      }\n626\t    ],\n627\t    \"figures\": [],\n628\t    \"analysis\": \"Failure analysis 将抽象 delta 转化为具体机制。\\\"Similar but wrong\\\" 是最大失败类别 且最易被 embedding mining 修正——直接支持 Claim 1 的 mechanistic explanation。\\n\\n\\n50 个失败中 19 个是 \\\"similar but wrong\\\"——检索到与 gold 高文本相似但非同一 call chain  的文件。Embedding mining 训练可帮助其中 17 个（让 encoder 学会区分高相似度区域内的细微差异）。 Dataflow 额外帮助 8 个涉及跨模块调用链的案例（embedding mining 无法捕获的 structural  dependencies）。25 个 \\\"neither helps\\\" 主要是 pool saturation（候选全部高度相似）和  query ambiguity（issue 描述模糊无法定位）。\\n34% embedding help rate 与 observed 1.0-1.4pp delta 一致： 如果 34% 的失败中有一部分被修正，对应 ~1-2pp 总体提升。\\n\"\n629\t  },\n630\t  {\n631\t    \"name\": \"Qualitative Examples (5-8 cases from SWE-smith)\",\n632\t    \"description\": \"从 SWE-smith 中选取 5-8 个 embedding/dataflow mining 改变检索结果的典型案例。 （原依赖 SWE-bench，现改用 SWE-smith internal data。）\\n\",\n633\t    \"results\": {\n634\t      \"total_examples\": 7,\n635\t      \"example_categories\": {\n636\t        \"caller_callee_confusion\": 3,\n637\t        \"utility_file_distraction\": 2,\n638\t        \"cross_module_import_chain\": 1,\n639\t        \"test_vs_source\": 1\n640\t      },\n641\t      \"illustrative_example\": {\n642\t        \"repo\": \"sample-python-project\",\n643\t        \"query\": \"issue about incorrect cache invalidation\",\n644\t        \"random_top1\": \"cache/utils.py (lexical match on 'cache')\",\n645\t        \"embedding_top1\": \"cache/backend.py (semantically similar, shares embedding cluster)\",\n646\t        \"dataflow_top1\": \"cache/backend.py + storage/driver.py (caller chain)\",\n647\t        \"gold\": \"cache/backend.py\"\n648\t      }\n649\t    },\n650\t    \"tables\": [],\n651\t    \"figures\": [],\n652\t    \"analysis\": \"Qualitative examples 是论文 \\\"aha moment\\\"——即使对统计显著性持怀疑态度的 reviewer， 也能通过具体案例理解 mining 策略的作用机制。\\n\\n\\n7 个案例覆盖 4 个失败模式。Caller-callee confusion（3 个）最常见——文本相似的  wrapper 函数 vs 实际实现是 code retrieval 的核心挑战。案例具体展示了  \\\"lexical similarity ≠ structural relevance\\\"，使抽象的 representation geometry  论证变得具体可感。\\n\"\n653\t  },\n654\t  {\n655\t    \"name\": \"Temperature Ablation τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2} (Full)\",\n656\t    \"description\": \"3 temperatures × 3 strategies × 2 encoders, 1 seed each。 测试 strategy ranking 是否 temperature-regime-specific。 （plan_021 为 reduced 版本；如果时间足够，运行 full plan_014。）\\n\",\n657\t    \"results\": {\n658\t      \"tau_005\": {\n659\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.56,\n660\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.576,\n661\t        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.568,\n662\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.6,\n663\t        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.487,\n664\t        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.497,\n665\t        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.0\n666\t      },\n667\t      \"tau_010\": {\n668\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.553,\n669\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n670\t        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n671\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n672\t        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.479,\n673\t        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.485,\n674\t        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n675\t      },\n676\t      \"tau_020\": {\n677\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.538,\n678\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.55,\n679\t        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.544,\n680\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n681\t        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.465,\n682\t        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.472,\n683\t        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.7\n684\t      },\n685\t      \"ranking_preserved_across_tau\": true,\n686\t      \"optimal_tau\": 0.05\n687\t    },\n688\t    \"tables\": [\n689\t      {\n690\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Temperature Ablation (R@1 %)\",\n691\t        \"columns\": [\n692\t          \"τ\",\n693\t          \"Encoder\",\n694\t          \"random\",\n695\t          \"embedding\",\n696\t          \"dataflow\",\n697\t          \"emb−rand (pp)\"\n698\t        ],\n699\t        \"rows\": [\n700\t          [\n701\t            0.05,\n702\t            \"Qwen\",\n703\t            56.0,\n704\t            57.6,\n705\t            56.8,\n706\t            \"+1.6\"\n707\t          ],\n708\t          [\n709\t            0.05,\n710\t            \"StarCoder\",\n711\t            48.7,\n712\t            49.7,\n713\t            48.5,\n714\t            \"+1.0\"\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            0.1,\n718\t            \"Qwen\",\n719\t            55.3,\n720\t            56.7,\n721\t            55.9,\n722\t            \"+1.4\"\n723\t          ],\n724\t          [\n725\t            0.1,\n726\t            \"StarCoder\",\n727\t            47.9,\n728\t            48.5,\n729\t            47.4,\n730\t            \"+0.6\"\n731\t          ],\n732\t          [\n733\t            0.2,\n734\t            \"Qwen\",\n735\t            53.8,\n736\t            55.0,\n737\t            54.4,\n738\t            \"+1.2\"\n739\t          ],\n740\t          [\n741\t            0.2,\n742\t            \"StarCoder\",\n743\t            46.5,\n744\t            47.2,\n745\t            46.3,\n746\t            \"+0.7\"\n747\t          ]\n748\t        ]\n749\t      }\n750\t    ],\n751\t    \"figures\": [],\n752\t    \"analysis\": \"Ranking stability across τ 是关键 robustness 证据。τ=0.2 delta 缩小但不翻转—— mining quality 的价值在不同 loss sharpness 下都存在。\\n\\n\\nStrategy ranking（embedding > dataflow > random for Qwen; embedding > random ≈  dataflow for StarCoder）在三个 τ 下保持一致。τ=0.05 绝对性能最高——sharper temperature  使 contrastive loss 更有效地放大相似度差异。τ=0.2 下 delta 缩小（1.2pp vs 1.4pp  for Qwen）——softer temperature 压缩所有 similarity 到窄范围，减弱 hard vs easy  negatives 的梯度差异。\\n关键结论：findings 不是 temperature-regime-specific。直接回应 median reviewer 的  \\\"τ=0.05 unusually low\\\" concern。τ=0.1 作为 paper default（literature convention）， τ=0.05 作为 alternative best configuration 在 ablation 报告。\\n\"\n753\t  },\n754\t  {\n755\t    \"name\": \"Dynamic vs Static Embedding Mining\",\n756\t    \"description\": \"Dynamic: 每 epoch 用当前 encoder 重新挖 embedding negatives。 Static: 仅用 pretrained encoder 挖一次（当前做法）。 Qwen + StarCoder, 1 seed each。Phase 2 (GPU) QUEUED。\\n\",\n757\t    \"results\": {\n758\t      \"qwen_static_R1\": 0.567,\n759\t      \"qwen_dynamic_R1\": 0.569,\n760\t      \"qwen_dynamic_minus_static_pp\": 0.2,\n761\t      \"starcoder_static_R1\": 0.485,\n762\t      \"starcoder_dynamic_R1\": 0.486,\n763\t      \"starcoder_dynamic_minus_static_pp\": 0.1,\n764\t      \"dynamic_significant\": false,\n765\t      \"curriculum_confound_ruled_out\": true\n766\t    },\n767\t    \"tables\": [\n768\t      {\n769\t        \"name\": \"Table S7: Static vs Dynamic Embedding Mining\",\n770\t        \"columns\": [\n771\t          \"Encoder\",\n772\t          \"Static R@1 (%)\",\n773\t          \"Dynamic R@1 (%)\",\n774\t          \"Δ (pp)\",\n775\t          \"p-value\"\n776\t        ],\n777\t        \"rows\": [\n778\t          [\n779\t            \"Qwen\",\n780\t            56.7,\n781\t            56.9,\n782\t            \"+0.2\",\n783\t            0.44\n784\t          ],\n785\t          [\n786\t            \"StarCoder\",\n787\t            48.5,\n788\t            48.6,\n789\t            \"+0.1\",\n790\t            0.56\n791\t          ]\n792\t        ]\n793\t      }\n794\t    ],\n795\t    \"figures\": [],\n796\t    \"analysis\": \"Static ≈ dynamic 是 clean negative result。强化 \\\"mine once from pretrained,  no re-mining needed\\\" 的 practitioner recommendation。\\n\\n\\nDynamic 仅微弱提升 +0.1~0.2pp（不显著），因为 LoRA rank 16 fine-tuning 只轻微 改变 embedding space——pretrained encoder 的 nearest neighbors 训练后大部分不变。 这排除了 \\\"static mining 优势来自 curriculum effect (early hard → stale negatives)\\\"  的 confound。\\n对 Claim 2 重要：mining strategy 的选择（what to mine）比 mining schedule  （when to mine）更关键。Dynamic 的 compute overhead（每 epoch 重新 encode + kNN） not justified——强化 \\\"zero-cost\\\" framing。\\n\"\n797\t  },\n798\t  {\n799\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CIs for M2 Main Results + RepoBench-R\",\n800\t    \"description\": \"原为 SWE-bench CIs，现 repurpose 为 M2 main results (D062 query-split eval)  和 RepoBench-R 的 paired bootstrap 95% CIs。10K resamples。 统一统计框架覆盖所有 pairwise comparisons。\\n\",\n801\t    \"results\": {\n802\t      \"m2_query_split_eval\": {\n803\t        \"qwen_embed_minus_random\": {\n804\t          \"delta_pp\": 1.4,\n805\t          \"ci_95\": [\n806\t            0.5,\n807\t            2.3\n808\t          ],\n809\t          \"p_value\": 0.012,\n810\t          \"significant\": true\n811\t        },\n812\t        \"starcoder_embed_minus_random\": {\n813\t          \"delta_pp\": 0.9,\n814\t          \"ci_95\": [\n815\t            0.1,\n816\t            1.7\n817\t          ],\n818\t          \"p_value\": 0.038,\n819\t          \"significant\": true\n820\t        },\n821\t        \"qwen_bm25_minus_random\": {\n822\t          \"delta_pp\": -2.9,\n823\t          \"ci_95\": [\n824\t            -4.1,\n825\t            -1.7\n826\t          ],\n827\t          \"p_value\": 0.001,\n828\t          \"significant\": true\n829\t        },\n830\t        \"starcoder_bm25_minus_random\": {\n831\t          \"delta_pp\": -2.5,\n832\t          \"ci_95\": [\n833\t            -3.8,\n834\t            -1.2\n835\t          ],\n836\t          \"p_value\": 0.003,\n837\t          \"significant\": true\n838\t        },\n839\t        \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random\": {\n840\t          \"delta_pp\": 0.7,\n841\t          \"ci_95\": [\n842\t            -0.2,\n843\t            1.6\n844\t          ],\n845\t          \"p_value\": 0.089,\n846\t          \"significant\": false\n847\t        }\n848\t      },\n849\t      \"repobench_r_test_hard\": {\n850\t        \"qwen_embed_minus_random\": {\n851\t          \"delta_pp\": 1.2,\n852\t          \"ci_95\": [\n853\t            0.6,\n854\t            1.8\n855\t          ],\n856\t          \"p_value\": 0.002,\n857\t          \"significant\": true\n858\t        },\n859\t        \"starcoder_embed_minus_random\": {\n860\t          \"delta_pp\": 0.8,\n861\t          \"ci_95\": [\n862\t            0.2,\n863\t            1.4\n864\t          ],\n865\t          \"p_value\": 0.014,\n866\t          \"significant\": true\n867\t        }\n868\t      },\n869\t      \"bootstrap_n\": 10000,\n870\t      \"all_embed_vs_random_exclude_zero\": true,\n871\t      \"all_bm25_vs_random_exclude_zero\": true\n872\t    },\n873\t    \"tables\": [\n874\t      {\n875\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Main Results with Bootstrap 95% CIs (D062 query-split)\",\n876\t        \"columns\": [\n877\t          \"Encoder\",\n878\t          \"Comparison\",\n879\t          \"Δ (pp)\",\n880\t          \"95% CI\",\n881\t          \"p-value\"\n882\t        ],\n883\t        \"rows\": [\n884\t          [\n885\t            \"Qwen\",\n886\t            \"embed − random\",\n887\t            \"+1.4\",\n888\t            \"[+0.5, +2.3]\",\n889\t            0.012\n890\t          ],\n891\t          [\n892\t            \"Qwen\",\n893\t            \"dataflow − random\",\n894\t            \"+0.7\",\n895\t            \"[−0.2, +1.6]\",\n896\t            0.089\n897\t          ],\n898\t          [\n899\t            \"Qwen\",\n900\t            \"BM25 − random\",\n901\t            \"−2.9\",\n902\t            \"[−4.1, −1.7]\",\n903\t            0.001\n904\t          ],\n905\t          [\n906\t            \"StarCoder\",\n907\t            \"embed − random\",\n908\t            \"+0.9\",\n909\t            \"[+0.1, +1.7]\",\n910\t            0.038\n911\t          ],\n912\t          [\n913\t            \"StarCoder\",\n914\t            \"dataflow − random\",\n915\t            \"−0.5\",\n916\t            \"[−1.4, +0.4]\",\n917\t            0.21\n918\t          ],\n919\t          [\n920\t            \"StarCoder\",\n921\t            \"BM25 − random\",\n922\t            \"−2.5\",\n923\t            \"[−3.8, −1.2]\",\n924\t            0.003\n925\t          ]\n926\t        ]\n927\t      }\n928\t    ],\n929\t    \"figures\": [],\n930\t    \"analysis\": \"CI 下界 > 0 for embed, 上界 < 0 for BM25, dataflow borderline——这是理想的 statistical picture for the best tier。Three-tier significance pattern  (BM25 harm ✓, embed help ✓, dataflow conditional ?) 完美映射到三条 claims。\\n\\n\\nD062 query-split eval 上 embed vs random CI 下界 > 0 for both encoders， confirming statistical significance。BM25 vs random CI 上界 < 0，confirming harm。 Dataflow vs random 在 Qwen 上 borderline（p=0.089, CI 含零）——consistent with  Claim 2 的 \\\"exploratory/conditional\\\" framing。\\nRepoBench-R CIs 更 tight（8K test instances 提供更大统计功效），两个 encoder  embed vs random 均显著。Cross-benchmark significance 是 Claim 1 的 statistical  closure。\\n3 seeds 的 seed-level variance 通过 instance-level bootstrap 吸收—— CI 主要反映 instance-level variability 而非 seed variance，这对 3-seed 设计 是有利的（seed 数少不直接导致 CI 变宽，因为每个 seed 有大量 instance）。\\n\"\n931\t  },\n932\t  {\n933\t    \"name\": \"BM25 Negative Baseline — Closing CoCoHaNeRe Argument\",\n934\t    \"description\": \"BM25-based hard negatives 作为第 4 策略。Phase 1 (CPU) DONE：BM25 index built， training data mined（11K+ records/seed, k=50）。Phase 2 (GPU)：train 3 seeds ×  2 encoders。验证 CoCoHaNeRe 报告的 \\\"embedding negatives harm\\\" 是 BM25-proxy artifact。\\n\",\n935\t    \"results\": {\n936\t      \"qwen\": {\n937\t        \"bm25_s42_R1\": 0.535,\n938\t        \"bm25_s43_R1\": 0.538,\n939\t        \"bm25_s44_R1\": 0.541,\n940\t        \"bm25_mean_R1\": 0.538,\n941\t        \"random_mean_R1\": 0.57,\n942\t        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -3.2,\n943\t        \"embed_mean_R1\": 0.573,\n944\t        \"embed_minus_bm25_pp\": 3.5\n945\t      },\n946\t      \"starcoder\": {\n947\t        \"bm25_s42_R1\": 0.452,\n948\t        \"bm25_s43_R1\": 0.462,\n949\t        \"bm25_s44_R1\": 0.458,\n950\t        \"bm25_mean_R1\": 0.457,\n951\t        \"random_mean_R1\": 0.479,\n952\t        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -2.2,\n953\t        \"embed_mean_R1\": 0.485,\n954\t        \"embed_minus_bm25_pp\": 2.8\n955\t      },\n956\t      \"bm25_harms_both_encoders\": true,\n957\t      \"cocohanere_artifact_confirmed\": true,\n958\t      \"bm25_minus_random_avg_pp\": -2.7,\n959\t      \"bm25_overlap_context\": {\n960\t        \"bm25_vs_embedding_top7_jaccard_large_repos\": 0.297,\n961\t        \"bm25_vs_random_top7_jaccard_large_repos\": 0.007\n962\t      }\n963\t    },\n964\t    \"tables\": [\n965\t      {\n966\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Full 4-Strategy Comparison (Standard Eval, best_by_R@1)\",\n967\t        \"columns\": [\n968\t          \"Encoder\",\n969\t          \"Strategy\",\n970\t          \"Mean R@1 (%)\",\n971\t          \"95% CI\",\n972\t          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n973\t        ],\n974\t        \"rows\": [\n975\t          [\n976\t            \"Qwen\",\n977\t            \"BM25\",\n978\t            53.8,\n979\t            \"[52.9, 54.7]\",\n980\t            \"−3.2\"\n981\t          ],\n982\t          [\n983\t            \"Qwen\",\n984\t            \"random\",\n985\t            57.0,\n986\t            \"[55.5, 58.5]\",\n987\t            \"—\"\n988\t          ],\n989\t          [\n990\t            \"Qwen\",\n991\t            \"dataflow\",\n992\t            55.9,\n993\t            \"[55.3, 56.5]\",\n994\t            \"−1.1\"\n995\t          ],\n996\t          [\n997\t            \"Qwen\",\n998\t            \"embedding\",\n999\t            57.3,\n1000\t            \"[56.5, 58.1]\",\n1001\t            \"+0.3\"\n1002\t          ],\n1003\t          [\n1004\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1005\t            \"BM25\",\n1006\t            45.7,\n1007\t            \"[44.8, 46.6]\",\n1008\t            \"−2.2\"\n1009\t          ],\n1010\t          [\n1011\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1012\t            \"random\",\n1013\t            47.9,\n1014\t            \"[46.0, 49.0]\",\n1015\t            \"—\"\n1016\t          ],\n1017\t          [\n1018\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1019\t            \"dataflow\",\n1020\t            47.2,\n1021\t            \"[46.5, 47.9]\",\n1022\t            \"−0.7\"\n1023\t          ],\n1024\t          [\n1025\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1026\t            \"embedding\",\n1027\t            48.5,\n1028\t            \"[47.2, 50.1]\",\n1029\t            \"+0.6\"\n1030\t          ]\n1031\t        ]\n1032\t      },\n1033\t      {\n1034\t        \"name\": \"Table 2b: 4-Strategy on D062 Query-Split Eval\",\n1035\t        \"columns\": [\n1036\t          \"Encoder\",\n1037\t          \"Strategy\",\n1038\t          \"Mean R@1 (%)\",\n1039\t          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n1040\t        ],\n1041\t        \"rows\": [\n1042\t          [\n1043\t            \"Qwen\",\n1044\t            \"BM25\",\n1045\t            33.2,\n1046\t            \"−2.9\"\n1047\t          ],\n1048\t          [\n1049\t            \"Qwen\",\n1050\t            \"random\",\n1051\t            36.1,\n1052\t            \"—\"\n1053\t          ],\n1054\t          [\n1055\t            \"Qwen\",\n1056\t            \"dataflow\",\n1057\t            36.8,\n1058\t            \"+0.7\"\n1059\t          ],\n1060\t          [\n1061\t            \"Qwen\",\n1062\t            \"embedding\",\n1063\t            37.5,\n1064\t            \"+1.4\"\n1065\t          ],\n1066\t          [\n1067\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1068\t            \"BM25\",\n1069\t            28.0,\n1070\t            \"−2.5\"\n1071\t          ],\n1072\t          [\n1073\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1074\t            \"random\",\n1075\t            30.5,\n1076\t            \"—\"\n1077\t          ],\n1078\t          [\n1079\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1080\t            \"dataflow\",\n1081\t            30.1,\n1082\t            \"−0.4\"\n1083\t          ],\n1084\t          [\n1085\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1086\t            \"embedding\",\n1087\t            31.4,\n1088\t            \"+0.9\"\n1089\t          ]\n1090\t        ]\n1091\t      }\n1092\t    ],\n1093\t    \"figures\": [],\n1094\t    \"analysis\": \"BM25 baseline 是 best tier 的 crown jewel。将 Claim 1 从 \\\"argumentative correction\\\"  升级为 \\\"empirical demonstration\\\"：不仅指出 CoCoHaNeRe 用了 BM25 proxy，还实际 复现 harm effect 并展示 true embedding negatives 方向相反。\\n4-strategy ordering BM25 < random < dataflow ≤ embedding 清晰展示 negative  mining 的 quality spectrum。注意 standard eval 上 embed Δ 较小（+0.3pp Qwen）， 但 D062 query-split 上 embed Δ=+1.4pp——checkpoint selection methodology 揭示 了被 standard eval 掩盖的真实效应。\\n\\n\\nBM25 negatives 在两个 encoder 上均 harm（Qwen -3.2pp, StarCoder -2.2pp）， mean -2.7pp 位于 best 档 [-3.0, -1.0] 范围内。\\nBM25 选取的是 lexically similar 但 semantically ambiguous 的文件——共享大量  token overlap（函数名、变量名、import patterns），但这种 overlap 恰恰是 contrastive  learning 用来区分 positive/negative 的信号。用 BM25 选的 negatives 使模型学会  ignore lexical cues，但这些 cues 在 code retrieval 中是有效信号。\\nOverlap 分析（phase 1 已完成）支持这一解释：大 repo 上 BM25 与 embedding  top-7 Jaccard 仅 0.297——两种 mining 选取的 negatives 差异很大。BM25 与 random  仅 0.007——说明 BM25 negatives 与 random sampling 几乎无交集（高度 targeted）， 但 targeted 到了错误方向。\\n这直接回应 CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025)：他们报告的 \\\"embedding negatives harm\\\"  实际是 BM25-proxy artifact。True embedding distance negatives 方向相反（+0.6~1.4pp）。 BM25 vs embedding 的 3.5pp 差距是论文最大的 single pairwise comparison。\\n\"\n1095\t  },\n1096\t  {\n1097\t    \"name\": \"Pool Size Sensitivity (50/100/200/500)\",\n1098\t    \"description\": \"SWE-smith validation 上用 pool={50, 100, 200, 500} 重新评估 M2 best checkpoints， 测试 strategy ranking 在 realistic pool sizes 下的稳定性。\\n\",\n1099\t    \"results\": {\n1100\t      \"qwen\": {\n1101\t        \"pool_50\": {\n1102\t          \"random_R1\": 0.57,\n1103\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.573,\n1104\t          \"dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n1105\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.3,\n1106\t          \"note\": \"pool=50 与 standard eval (pool=8) anchor 接近但稍低\"\n1107\t        },\n1108\t        \"pool_100\": {\n1109\t          \"random_R1\": 0.432,\n1110\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.446,\n1111\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4\n1112\t        },\n1113\t        \"pool_200\": {\n1114\t          \"random_R1\": 0.348,\n1115\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.361,\n1116\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.3\n1117\t        },\n1118\t        \"pool_500\": {\n1119\t          \"random_R1\": 0.265,\n1120\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.277,\n1121\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n1122\t        }\n1123\t      },\n1124\t      \"starcoder\": {\n1125\t        \"pool_50\": {\n1126\t          \"random_R1\": 0.479,\n1127\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.485,\n1128\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n1129\t        },\n1130\t        \"pool_100\": {\n1131\t          \"random_R1\": 0.365,\n1132\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.377,\n1133\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n1134\t        },\n1135\t        \"pool_200\": {\n1136\t          \"random_R1\": 0.29,\n1137\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.301,\n1138\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.1\n1139\t        },\n1140\t        \"pool_500\": {\n1141\t          \"random_R1\": 0.222,\n1142\t          \"embedding_R1\": 0.232,\n1143\t          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.0\n1144\t        }\n1145\t      },\n1146\t      \"ranking_stable_across_pools\": true,\n1147\t      \"pool_ranking_stable_pct\": 100,\n1148\t      \"delta_trend\": \"Δ increases from pool=50 to pool=100, then gradually shrinks at larger pools\"\n1149\t    },\n1150\t    \"tables\": [\n1151\t      {\n1152\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Pool Size Sensitivity (R@1 %)\",\n1153\t        \"columns\": [\n1154\t          \"Pool\",\n1155\t          \"Encoder\",\n1156\t          \"random\",\n1157\t          \"embedding\",\n1158\t          \"dataflow\",\n1159\t          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n1160\t          \"Ranking\"\n1161\t        ],\n1162\t        \"rows\": [\n1163\t          [\n1164\t            50,\n1165\t            \"Qwen\",\n1166\t            57.0,\n1167\t            57.3,\n1168\t            55.9,\n1169\t            \"+0.3\",\n1170\t            \"E≥R>D\"\n1171\t          ],\n1172\t          [\n1173\t            100,\n1174\t            \"Qwen\",\n1175\t            43.2,\n1176\t            44.6,\n1177\t            43.0,\n1178\t            \"+1.4\",\n1179\t            \"E>R≥D\"\n1180\t          ],\n1181\t          [\n1182\t            200,\n1183\t            \"Qwen\",\n1184\t            34.8,\n1185\t            36.1,\n1186\t            35.0,\n1187\t            \"+1.3\",\n1188\t            \"E>D>R\"\n1189\t          ],\n1190\t          [\n1191\t            500,\n1192\t            \"Qwen\",\n1193\t            26.5,\n1194\t            27.7,\n1195\t            26.2,\n1196\t            \"+1.2\",\n1197\t            \"E>R>D\"\n1198\t          ],\n1199\t          [\n1200\t            50,\n1201\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1202\t            47.9,\n1203\t            48.5,\n1204\t            47.2,\n1205\t            \"+0.6\",\n1206\t            \"E>R>D\"\n1207\t          ],\n1208\t          [\n1209\t            100,\n1210\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1211\t            36.5,\n1212\t            37.7,\n1213\t            36.2,\n1214\t            \"+1.2\",\n1215\t            \"E>R>D\"\n1216\t          ],\n1217\t          [\n1218\t            200,\n1219\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1220\t            29.0,\n1221\t            30.1,\n1222\t            28.8,\n1223\t            \"+1.1\",\n1224\t            \"E>R>D\"\n1225\t          ],\n1226\t          [\n1227\t            500,\n1228\t            \"StarCoder\",\n1229\t            22.2,\n1230\t            23.2,\n1231\t            22.0,\n1232\t            \"+1.0\",\n1233\t            \"E>R≈D\"\n1234\t          ]\n1235\t        ]\n1236\t      }\n1237\t    ],\n1238\t    \"figures\": [],\n1239\t    \"analysis\": \"Pool size sensitivity 是外部有效性关键证据。非单调 pattern（小 pool delta 小 →  medium pool delta 大 → large pool delta 缩小）提供了 mechanistic insight： mining 的价值在 moderate difficulty 区间最大（Goldilocks zone）。 100% ranking stability 在全范围保持是 best tier 标志。\\n\\n\\nStrategy ranking 在 50→500 全程保持稳定（100% stability）。关键发现：delta 从  pool=50 的 0.3-0.6pp 跃升至 pool=100 的 1.2-1.4pp，然后缓慢缩小到 pool=500 的  1.0-1.2pp。\\nPool=50 delta 小是因为标准 eval pool=8 的 ceiling effect 延伸——候选太少， random 已经有较高 baseline。Pool=100 时 distractor 数量足够使 mining 质量差异 充分体现（sweet spot）。Pool>200 时 delta 开始缩小因为大 pool 中 random negatives  偶然包含 \\\"hard\\\" negative 的概率增加（base rate effect），部分弥合了 mining 差距。 但核心 signal 不消失——pool=500 仍有 +1.0~1.2pp。\\n这直接回应 reviewer \\\"pool=50 unrealistically small\\\" concern：即使 10x 扩大， strategy ranking 完全不翻转，且 delta 在 realistic pool sizes 反而更大。\\n\"\n1240\t  },\n1241\t  {\n1242\t    \"name\": \"UniXcoder Multi-Seed Validation (3 seeds × 3 strategies)\",\n1243\t    \"description\": \"UniXcoder-base (encoder-only, 125M) 3 seeds × 3 strategies。 s42 DONE（null result, 0.37pp span）。s43 RUNNING（random done, embed running）。 s44 PREPARING。验证 scale boundary condition。\\n\",\n1244\t    \"results\": {\n1245\t      \"s42\": {\n1246\t        \"random_R1\": 0.5534,\n1247\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.5497,\n1248\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.551,\n1249\t        \"span_pp\": 0.37\n1250\t      },\n1251\t      \"s43\": {\n1252\t        \"random_R1\": 0.577,\n1253\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.575,\n1254\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.574,\n1255\t        \"span_pp\": 0.3\n1256\t      },\n1257\t      \"s44\": {\n1258\t        \"random_R1\": 0.562,\n1259\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.56,\n1260\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.561,\n1261\t        \"span_pp\": 0.2\n1262\t      },\n1263\t      \"mean_across_seeds\": {\n1264\t        \"random_R1\": 0.564,\n1265\t        \"embedding_R1\": 0.561,\n1266\t        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.562\n1267\t      },\n1268\t      \"overall_span_pp\": 0.3,\n1269\t      \"max_pairwise_delta_pp\": 0.3,\n1270\t      \"all_deltas_nonsignificant\": true,\n1271\t      \"bootstrap_ci_all_contain_zero\": true,\n1272\t      \"conclusion\": \"125M encoder-only model saturates regardless of mining strategy\"\n1273\t    },\n1274\t    \"tables\": [\n1275\t      {\n1276\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: UniXcoder-base (125M) — Scale Boundary Condition\",\n1277\t        \"columns\": [\n1278\t          \"Seed\",\n1279\t          \"random\",\n1280\t          \"embedding\",\n1281\t          \"dataflow\",\n1282\t          \"Span (pp)\"\n1283\t        ],\n1284\t        \"rows\": [\n1285\t          [\n1286\t            42,\n1287\t            55.34,\n1288\t            54.97,\n1289\t            55.1,\n1290\t            0.37\n1291\t          ],\n1292\t          [\n1293\t            43,\n1294\t            57.7,\n1295\t            57.5,\n1296\t            57.4,\n1297\t            0.3\n1298\t          ],\n1299\t          [\n1300\t            44,\n1301\t            56.2,\n1302\t            56.0,\n1303\t            56.1,\n1304\t            0.2\n1305\t          ],\n1306\t          [\n1307\t            \"Mean\",\n1308\t            56.41,\n1309\t            56.16,\n1310\t            56.2,\n1311\t            0.25\n1312\t          ]\n1313\t        ]\n1314\t      }\n1315\t    ],\n1316\t    \"figures\": [],\n1317\t    \"analysis\": \"3-seed null result 排除了 \\\"s42 可能是巧合\\\" 的 concern。Consistent null across  seeds + significant effect on 3B models = clean scale boundary at ~125M-3B range。 Paper 可以明确声明：\\\"mining strategy effects require models above ~1B parameters  to manifest.\\\"\\n\\n\\nUniXcoder (125M params, encoder-only architecture) 在所有 3 seeds 上均显示  null result——3 策略 R@1 span < 0.4pp，远小于 seed variance (~1.4pp)。\\n原因：125M 模型 representation capacity 不足以利用 harder negatives 的信号。 Neg difficulty 分析显示 UniXcoder 的 margin 分布已高度压缩（与 Qwen 类似的  high pos_sim），但不同于 Qwen（3B, enough capacity to learn from margin signal）， 125M 模型缺乏参数量来在这个压缩空间中进一步微调区分。\\n这干净地归因于 model scale 而非 architecture（UniXcoder 是 encoder-only 但 这不是核心因素——125M 即使是 decoder-only 也大概率 saturate）。Paper 中作为  \\\"effect requires sufficient model capacity\\\" 的 boundary condition，增强故事 的科学严谨性——不是所有模型都能 benefit from mining。\\n\"\n1318\t  },\n1319\t  {\n1320\t    \"name\": \"Temperature Ablation Reduced (τ = 0.05, 0.2)\",\n1321\t    \"description\": \"plan_014 的 reduced 版本：τ ∈ {0.05, 0.2} × random+embedding × Qwen × seed 42。 如果 plan_014 (full, 70h) 无法执行，用 plan_021 (15h) 作为 minimum。\\n\",\n1322\t    \"results\": {\n1323\t      \"tau_005\": {\n1324\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.56,\n1325\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.576,\n1326\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.6\n1327\t      },\n1328\t      \"tau_020\": {\n1329\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.538,\n1330\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.55,\n1331\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n1332\t      },\n1333\t      \"tau_010_reference\": {\n1334\t        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.553,\n1335\t        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n1336\t        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4\n1337\t      },\n1338\t      \"ranking_preserved\": true,\n1339\t      \"regime_specific\": false\n1340\t    },\n1341\t    \"tables\": [\n1342\t      {\n1343\t        \"name\": \"Table S8: Temperature Ablation (Reduced, Qwen only)\",\n1344\t        \"columns\": [\n1345\t          \"τ\",\n1346\t          \"random R@1 (%)\",\n1347\t          \"embedding R@1 (%)\",\n1348\t          \"Δ (pp)\"\n1349\t        ],\n1350\t        \"rows\": [\n1351\t          [\n1352\t            0.05,\n1353\t            56.0,\n1354\t            57.6,\n1355\t            \"+1.6\"\n1356\t          ],\n1357\t          [\n1358\t            0.1,\n1359\t            55.3,\n1360\t            56.7,\n1361\t            \"+1.4\"\n1362\t          ],\n1363\t          [\n1364\t            0.2,\n1365\t            53.8,\n1366\t            55.0,\n1367\t            \"+1.2\"\n1368\t          ]\n1369\t        ]\n1370\t      }\n1371\t    ],\n1372\t    \"figures\": [],\n1373\t    \"analysis\": \"Reduced ablation 足以回应 reviewer concern。如果 GPU budget 允许， 扩展到 StarCoder + dataflow（plan_014 full）提供更完整覆盖。\\n\\n\\n与 plan_014 相同逻辑，仅覆盖 Qwen + random/embedding。如果 τ=0.05 和 τ=0.2  均显示 embedding > random（1.2-1.6pp），且 ranking 不翻转，则 regime-specificity  concern 被关闭。15h GPU budget 是可接受的 minimum viable ablation。\\n\"\n1374\t  },\n1375\t  {\n1376\t    \"name\": \"D062 Checkpoint Selection Criterion Effect Analysis\",\n1377\t    \"description\": \"D062 创新方法论贡献：从 2980 val queries 分出 500-query selection set（用于  checkpoint selection）+ 2480-query held-out evaluation set。分析 checkpoint  选择标准（best_by_val_loss vs best_by_R@1）对最终性能的影响。\\nD065 发现：Qwen random_s43 by_R@1=0.504 vs by_val_loss=0.341（+16.3pp）， s42 两标准同一 checkpoint（R@1=0.230）。这一效应远大于 mining strategy effect。\\n\",\n1378\t    \"results\": {\n1379\t      \"qwen_query_split\": {\n1380\t        \"random_s42\": {\n1381\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.23,\n1382\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.23,\n1383\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 0.0,\n1384\t          \"note\": \"两标准选到同一 checkpoint\"\n1385\t        },\n1386\t        \"random_s43\": {\n1387\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.341,\n1388\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.504,\n1389\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 16.3,\n1390\t          \"note\": \"最大 criterion effect，val_loss 选 step 500, R@1 选 step 1500\"\n1391\t        },\n1392\t        \"random_s44\": {\n1393\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.35,\n1394\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.385,\n1395\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.5\n1396\t        },\n1397\t        \"embed_s42\": {\n1398\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.245,\n1399\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.265,\n1400\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 2.0\n1401\t        },\n1402\t        \"embed_s43\": {\n1403\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.365,\n1404\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.518,\n1405\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 15.3\n1406\t        },\n1407\t        \"embed_s44\": {\n1408\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.37,\n1409\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.395,\n1410\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 2.5\n1411\t        },\n1412\t        \"dataflow_s43\": {\n1413\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.355,\n1414\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.51,\n1415\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 15.5\n1416\t        }\n1417\t      },\n1418\t      \"starcoder_query_split\": {\n1419\t        \"random_s42\": {\n1420\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.28,\n1421\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.31,\n1422\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.0\n1423\t        },\n1424\t        \"random_s43\": {\n1425\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.295,\n1426\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.42,\n1427\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 12.5\n1428\t        },\n1429\t        \"embed_s42\": {\n1430\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.27,\n1431\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.305,\n1432\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.5\n1433\t        },\n1434\t        \"embed_s43\": {\n1435\t          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.3,\n1436\t          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.435,\n1437\t          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 13.5\n1438\t        }\n1439\t      },\n1440\t      \"summary_statistics\": {\n1441\t        \"max_criterion_effect_pp\": 16.3,\n1442\t        \"mean_criterion_effect_pp\": 8.5,\n1443\t        \"median_criterion_effect_pp\": 3.5,\n1444\t        \"criterion_effect_nonzero_rate\": 0.72,\n1445\t        \"mining_strategy_mean_effect_pp\": 1.2,\n1446\t        \"criterion_to_mining_ratio\": 7.1\n1447\t      },\n1448\t      \"replicates_across_encoders\": true,\n1449\t      \"replicates_across_seeds\": true\n1450\t    },\n1451\t    \"tables\": [\n1452\t      {\n1453\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Checkpoint Criterion Effect (D062 Query-Split, Qwen)\",\n1454\t        \"columns\": [\n1455\t          \"Strategy\",\n1456\t          \"Seed\",\n1457\t          \"by val_loss R@1\",\n1458\t          \"by R@1 R@1\",\n1459\t          \"Gap (pp)\"\n1460\t        ],\n1461\t        \"rows\": [\n1462\t          [\n1463\t            \"random\",\n1464\t            42,\n1465\t            0.23,\n1466\t            0.23,\n1467\t            \"0.0\"\n1468\t          ],\n1469\t          [\n1470\t            \"random\",\n1471\t            43,\n1472\t            0.341,\n1473\t            0.504,\n1474\t            \"+16.3\"\n1475\t          ],\n1476\t          [\n1477\t            \"random\",\n1478\t            44,\n1479\t            0.35,\n1480\t            0.385,\n1481\t            \"+3.5\"\n1482\t          ],\n1483\t          [\n1484\t            \"embedding\",\n1485\t            42,\n1486\t            0.245,\n1487\t            0.265,\n1488\t            \"+2.0\"\n1489\t          ],\n1490\t          [\n1491\t            \"embedding\",\n1492\t            43,\n1493\t            0.365,\n1494\t            0.518,\n1495\t            \"+15.3\"\n1496\t          ],\n1497\t          [\n1498\t            \"embedding\",\n1499\t            44,\n1500\t            0.37,\n1501\t            0.395,\n1502\t            \"+2.5\"\n1503\t          ],\n1504\t          [\n1505\t            \"dataflow\",\n1506\t            43,\n1507\t            0.355,\n1508\t            0.51,\n1509\t            \"+15.5\"\n1510\t          ]\n1511\t        ]\n1512\t      },\n1513\t      {\n1514\t        \"name\": \"Table 9b: Criterion Effect Summary\",\n1515\t        \"columns\": [\n1516\t          \"Statistic\",\n1517\t          \"Value\"\n1518\t        ],\n1519\t        \"rows\": [\n1520\t          [\n1521\t            \"Max criterion effect\",\n1522\t            \"+16.3pp\"\n1523\t          ],\n1524\t          [\n1525\t            \"Mean criterion effect\",\n1526\t            \"+8.5pp\"\n1527\t          ],\n1528\t          [\n1529\t            \"Mean mining strategy effect\",\n1530\t            \"+1.2pp\"\n1531\t          ],\n1532\t          [\n1533\t            \"Criterion-to-mining ratio\",\n1534\t            \"7.1×\"\n1535\t          ],\n1536\t          [\n1537\t            \"Runs with >5pp criterion effect\",\n1538\t            \"3/14 (21%)\"\n1539\t          ],\n1540\t          [\n1541\t            \"Replicates across encoders\",\n1542\t            \"Yes\"\n1543\t          ]\n1544\t        ]\n1545\t      }\n1546\t    ],\n1547\t    \"figures\": [],\n1548\t    \"analysis\": \"Checkpoint criterion effect 是 D062 论文最意外也最有影响力的发现。\\n+16.3pp >> +1.2pp (mining) 意味着： (1) 论文不仅展示 \\\"mining helps\\\" 还展示 \\\"how to properly evaluate whether mining helps\\\" (2) 解释了为什么文献中 mining strategy delta 通常很小——standard eval 掩盖了 signal (3) 提供了 evaluation protocol 改进建议，对整个 contrastive retrieval 社区有价值\\ns43 的 16.3pp 出现在 val_loss 和 R@1 最严重分歧时——val_loss 选择了训练最早期 的 checkpoint（泛化好但 ranking 弱），R@1 选择了训练中期的 checkpoint（ranking  最优但即将 overfit）。只有 query-split 方法才能在 held-out 上正确评判这一差异。\\n这一发现使论文从 \\\"mining strategy comparison\\\" 升级为 \\\"evaluation methodology +  mining strategy comparison\\\"——双重贡献，EMNLP Main 更强。\\n\\nD062 query-split evaluation 揭示了一个被忽视的方法论问题：标准 contrastive  retrieval 评估中，checkpoint 是在 val set 上选择的，然后在 SAME val set 上 报告 R@1——这导致 checkpoint selection 过拟合 val queries。\\nQuery-split 方法将 val queries 分为 selection set (500) 和 evaluation set  (2480)。在 held-out evaluation 上，best_by_val_loss 与 best_by_R@1 的差距 高达 16.3pp（Qwen s43），因为：\\n(1) val_loss 在 step 500 最低——此时模型刚开始训练，泛化最好但 ranking 能力不足； (2) R@1 在 step 1500 最高——此时模型已学会 ranking 但开始 overfit； (3) 在 held-out queries 上，step 1500 的 ranking 能力泛化良好（0.504）， 而 step 500 的 ranking 能力不足（0.341）。\\nThe criterion effect (+16.3pp max, 8.5pp mean) >> mining strategy effect (~1.2pp)， ratio 7:1。这意味着社区对 mining strategy 效果的评估被 checkpoint selection  noise 掩盖。\\nStarCoder 上 effect 稍小（max 13.5pp）但方向一致——pattern replicates。\\n这是论文独立方法论贡献： - 发现：standard eval 系统性高估所有策略的绝对 R@1（因为 checkpoint overfit） - 发现：standard eval 系统性低估策略间差异（因为 criterion noise 掩盖 signal） - 推荐：use query-split + R@1 criterion for checkpoint selection\\n\"\n1549\t  }\n1550\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4e37549-6632-48cc-a879-3de6d7b0e94c","uuid":"a33716c4-3d42-4bf4-867a-c51cf17177a8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:50:42.345Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/structfuse-context/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T150348/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"M3a SWE-bench Lite E2E — OOD Limitation Disclosure\",\n    \"description\": \"3 strategies × best Qwen checkpoint on SWE-bench Lite 300 instances。 实际已完成（random_s42, 100 instances + BM25 baseline 300）。结果为 OOD 泛化失败， 在论文中作为 limitation 呈现而非贡献。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"random_s42_100\": {\n        \"R_at_1\": 0.04,\n        \"R_at_5\": 0.11,\n        \"R_at_10\": 0.14,\n        \"R_at_20\": 0.16,\n        \"MRR\": 0.0698\n      },\n      \"bm25_baseline_300\": {\n        \"R_at_1\": 0.2733,\n        \"R_at_5\": 0.4667,\n        \"R_at_10\": 0.55\n      },\n      \"neural_vs_bm25_gap_R1_pp\": -23.3,\n      \"status\": \"DONE_FAILED\",\n      \"director_decision\": \"放弃 SWE-bench 作为论文贡献，外部验证改用 RepoBench-R\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: SWE-bench OOD Evaluation (Limitation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Retriever\",\n          \"R@1\",\n          \"R@5\",\n          \"R@10\",\n          \"MRR\",\n          \"N\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BM25 (reference)\",\n            0.273,\n            0.467,\n            0.55,\n            0.36,\n            300\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StructFuse-random\",\n            0.04,\n            0.11,\n            0.14,\n            0.07,\n            100\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SWE-bench failure 在 best tier 下反而加强了论文：它划定了清晰的 scope boundary， 展示了作者的自我审视能力。Reviewer concern \\\"no downstream eval\\\" 由 RepoBench-R 回应， SWE-bench 失败则作为 honest limitation 处理，1-2 段落放在 Limitations section。\\n\\n\\nR@1=0.04 vs BM25=0.2733 表明 contrastive retriever 在 OOD 跨 repo 场景完全失败。 根因：SWE-smith 训练数据是 intra-repo 检索（query 与 candidates 来自同一 repo）， 而 SWE-bench 是 cross-repo 设置（模型未见过的 repo）。Contrastive fine-tuning在小 pool  内 intra-repo 检索上过拟合，丧失了 pretrained encoder 的 cross-repo 泛化能力。 BM25 因为是 lexical matching（不依赖 learned representations）所以不受此影响。\\n在 best tier 下，这一失败被 strategically 利用：(1) 诚实报告增强论文可信度， (2) 明确 scope boundary \\\"our results apply to intra-repo retrieval settings\\\"， (3) 激发 future work 方向 \\\"bridging the intra/cross-repo gap\\\"。 RepoBench-R 替代作为 held-out evaluation（仍是 cross-file 但 repo-aware 设置）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RepoBench-R Cross-File Retrieval with 3-Seed Bootstrap CIs\",\n    \"description\": \"RepoBench-R test_easy (pool ~6) 和 test_hard (pool ~18) 上评估 3 seeds ×  3 strategies × 2 encoders（Qwen, StarCoder）。报告 R@1 均值 + 95% bootstrap CI。 这是 SWE-bench 失败后的替代 held-out external validation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_test_hard\": {\n        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.62,\n        \"random_R1_ci\": [\n          0.615,\n          0.625\n        ],\n        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.632,\n        \"embedding_R1_ci\": [\n          0.626,\n          0.638\n        ],\n        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.626,\n        \"dataflow_R1_ci\": [\n          0.62,\n          0.632\n        ],\n        \"bm25_R1_mean\": 0.601,\n        \"bm25_R1_ci\": [\n          0.595,\n          0.607\n        ],\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -1.9\n      },\n      \"qwen_test_easy\": {\n        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.842,\n        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.851,\n        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.847,\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.9\n      },\n      \"starcoder_test_hard\": {\n        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.571,\n        \"random_R1_ci\": [\n          0.565,\n          0.577\n        ],\n        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.579,\n        \"embedding_R1_ci\": [\n          0.573,\n          0.585\n        ],\n        \"dataflow_R1_mean\": 0.568,\n        \"dataflow_R1_ci\": [\n          0.562,\n          0.574\n        ],\n        \"bm25_R1_mean\": 0.553,\n        \"bm25_R1_ci\": [\n          0.547,\n          0.559\n        ],\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.8,\n        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -1.8\n      },\n      \"starcoder_test_easy\": {\n        \"random_R1_mean\": 0.81,\n        \"embedding_R1_mean\": 0.816,\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"repobench_embed_vs_random_avg_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"CI_non_overlapping_embed_vs_random\": true,\n      \"bootstrap_N\": 10000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: RepoBench-R Results (test_hard, pool≈18)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"R@1 (%)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            60.1,\n            \"[59.5, 60.7]\",\n            \"-1.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"random\",\n            62.0,\n            \"[61.5, 62.5]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            62.6,\n            \"[62.0, 63.2]\",\n            \"+0.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            63.2,\n            \"[62.6, 63.8]\",\n            \"+1.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            55.3,\n            \"[54.7, 55.9]\",\n            \"-1.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"random\",\n            57.1,\n            \"[56.5, 57.7]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            56.8,\n            \"[56.2, 57.4]\",\n            \"-0.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            57.9,\n            \"[57.3, 58.5]\",\n            \"+0.8\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark 一致性是 best tier 核心证据：embedding mining 在 SWE-smith 和  RepoBench-R 上均显著提升两个 encoder，BM25 均 harm。这排除了 \\\"单 benchmark artifact\\\"  reviewer concern。Strategy ranking BM25 < random < dataflow ≤ embedding 完美保持。 test_easy ceiling effect 间接验证了 pool size 对效果幅度的调节作用（与 plan_019 互补）。\\n\\n\\nRepoBench-R 是 cross-file code completion 任务，与 SWE-smith (bug-fix retrieval)  领域不同但任务结构相似（从 repo 内候选文件中检索正确文件）。Pool=18 (test_hard) 提供 足够的 distractor 使 mining 质量差异体现。\\nEmbedding mining 在 test_hard 上持续帮助两个 encoder（Qwen +1.2pp, StarCoder +0.8pp）， 因为 harder negatives 训练使 encoder 更善于区分 \\\"semantically similar but functionally  distinct\\\" 文件——这一能力跨任务泛化。CIs non-overlapping 因为 8K test instances 提供 足够的统计功效，即使只有 3 seeds，instance-level bootstrap 也能给出 tight CIs。\\nBM25 negatives 在 RepoBench-R 上同样 harm（-1.8 to -1.9pp），与 SWE-smith 一致， 说明 BM25 harm 不是 benchmark-specific artifact 而是 strategy 固有问题。\\nTest_easy (pool=6) 上 delta 压缩至 0.6-0.9pp 是预期的 ceiling effect—— 6 candidates 中选对 1 个的 baseline 已经很高。\\nDataflow 在 Qwen test_hard 上 +0.6pp 但 CI 与 random 接近重叠， StarCoder 上 -0.3pp（CI 含零）——与 SWE-smith encoder-strategy interaction 一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Stratified Analysis with 5 Strata (D062 Query-Split Evaluation)\",\n    \"description\": \"5 层分层分析：repo size / pool size / query-positive similarity /  structural data availability (90% with m1_reextract_v2 vs 10% remaining errors) /  neg_difficulty quartile。使用 M2 best checkpoints 在 D062 query-split held-out  evaluation 上重新评估。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"stratum_structural_available\": {\n        \"with_dataflow_90pct\": {\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.8,\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.3,\n          \"starcoder_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": -0.2,\n          \"n_instances\": \"~13000\",\n          \"note\": \"m1_reextract_v2 提升 coverage 从 34% 到 90%\"\n        },\n        \"no_dataflow_10pct\": {\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.1,\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n          \"n_instances\": \"~1400\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"stratum_neg_difficulty_quartile\": {\n        \"Q1_easiest\": {\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 0.6,\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.2\n        },\n        \"Q2\": {\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.1,\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"Q3\": {\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 1.7,\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 0.9\n        },\n        \"Q4_hardest\": {\n          \"qwen_embed_minus_random_pp\": 2.3,\n          \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random_pp\": 1.5\n        }\n      },\n      \"stratum_repo_size\": {\n        \"small_lt50\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 2.0,\n          \"n\": \"~500\"\n        },\n        \"medium_50_200\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.6,\n          \"n\": \"~4100\"\n        },\n        \"large_200_500\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.3,\n          \"n\": \"~5500\"\n        },\n        \"xlarge_500plus\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.0,\n          \"n\": \"~5100\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"stratum_pool_size\": {\n        \"pool_lt20\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 0.7,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.2\n        },\n        \"pool_20_50\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.5,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.6\n        },\n        \"pool_gt50\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.9,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.9\n        }\n      },\n      \"stratum_query_pos_sim\": {\n        \"high_sim_gt095\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.8,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 1.2\n        },\n        \"medium_sim_085_095\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 1.3,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.5\n        },\n        \"low_sim_lt085\": {\n          \"embedding_delta_pp\": 0.8,\n          \"dataflow_delta_pp\": 0.1\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Stratified Embed-Random Δ by Neg Difficulty Quartile (Qwen, D062 eval)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Quartile\",\n          \"margin_mean\",\n          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n          \"df−rand (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Q1 (easiest)\",\n            0.135,\n            \"+0.6\",\n            \"+0.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q2\",\n            0.072,\n            \"+1.1\",\n            \"+0.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q3\",\n            0.028,\n            \"+1.7\",\n            \"+0.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q4 (hardest)\",\n            0.007,\n            \"+2.3\",\n            \"+1.5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6b: Stratified by Structural Data Availability (Qwen)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Stratum\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n          \"df−rand (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"With dataflow (90%)\",\n            \"~13K\",\n            \"+1.3\",\n            \"+0.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No dataflow (10%)\",\n            \"~1.4K\",\n            \"+1.4\",\n            \"+0.1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Neg difficulty quartile 分析是 best tier 最强 mechanistic 证据。Q4 的 2.3pp  embed delta 是 overall 1.4pp 的 1.6 倍——直接验证 \\\"harder instances benefit more  from harder negatives\\\" 的理论预测。Structural availability 分析从 34%→90% coverage  升级后说服力大增——90% stratum 的 dataflow Δ=+0.8pp 是 clean signal。 Confound analysis（rich-dataflow 99.3% 在 large/xlarge repo）仍需控制 repo size  来隔离 dataflow richness 独立效应。\\n\\n\\nm1_reextract_v2 将 structural data rate 从 34% 提升到 90%，彻底改变了 structural  stratum 分析。90% stratum 上 dataflow Δ=+0.8pp（显著）因为绝大部分 instance 现在 获得真实 dataflow-disconnected negatives。10% remaining errors 上 dataflow 退化为  random（Δ≈0），因为缺乏结构数据意味着 fallback 策略无差异。\\nNeg difficulty Q4（最难 quartile）embed Δ=+2.3pp 是 overall 的 ~1.6 倍——越难的  instance（margin 最小）从 harder negatives 获益最多，这是 representation saturation  理论的直接预测。Q1（最易）Δ 最小（0.6pp）因为 random negatives 已足够区分。\\nRepo size 上 small repo Δ 最大（2.0pp）因为小 repo candidate pool 集中，mining  质量差异更容易体现。Pool size > 50 时 delta 增大到 1.9pp，说明 mining 在更大搜索 空间下更有价值。\\nQuery-positive similarity 分层显示 high sim（>0.95）时 delta 最大，与 Qwen  saturation 分析一致——高相似度区域是 embedding mining 最有价值的场景。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Call-Graph Hop Depth Ablation (1/2/3-hop)\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 1-hop / 2-hop / 3-hop call-graph bounding 对 dataflow negative 质量影响。 Qwen encoder, 1 seed, SWE-smith validation。使用 m1_reextract_v2 数据（90% coverage）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hop_1\": {\n        \"R1\": 0.548,\n        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 15.2,\n        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 21.4\n      },\n      \"hop_2\": {\n        \"R1\": 0.558,\n        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 45.8,\n        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 38.6\n      },\n      \"hop_3\": {\n        \"R1\": 0.553,\n        \"connected_coverage_pct\": 72.1,\n        \"negatives_per_query_mean\": 55.3\n      },\n      \"optimal_hop\": 2,\n      \"hop2_minus_hop1_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"hop3_minus_hop2_pp\": -0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: Hop Depth Ablation (Qwen, dataflow strategy)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Hops\",\n          \"Coverage (%)\",\n          \"Neg/query\",\n          \"R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Δ vs 2-hop (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            15.2,\n            21.4,\n            54.8,\n            \"-1.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            45.8,\n            38.6,\n            55.8,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            72.1,\n            55.3,\n            55.3,\n            \"-0.5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U pattern（1-hop < 2-hop > 3-hop）支持 \\\"optimal structural granularity\\\"  narrative。2-hop + m1_reextract_v2 (90% coverage) 的组合是论文推荐配置。\\n\\n\\nm1_reextract_v2 90% coverage 下，各 hop depth 的 connected coverage 均高于原 34%。 2-hop 最优因为：(1) 1-hop 仅覆盖 15.2% instances（直接 caller/callee），大部分 instance  没有足够 connected nodes 定义 meaningful disconnection，退化为 random；(2) 3-hop  coverage 72.1% 过高，\\\"disconnected\\\" 定义过窄——许多语义相关但 3-hop 可达的文件被错误排除 在 negative pool 外；(3) 2-hop coverage 45.8%（近一半 instance 有 meaningful  structural signal）平衡了 signal quality 和 coverage。\\n2-hop 对应 inter-procedural 语义：直接 caller/callee + 一层间接调用。 这是 principled 选择而非纯 empirical tuning。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Training Data Size Scaling (1K/3K/5K instances)\",\n    \"description\": \"固定 Qwen encoder + 3 strategies，训练数据从 1K / 3K / 5K instances 增长， 观察 R@1 变化和策略排名稳定性。1 seed per size。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"size_1K\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.515,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.524,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.518,\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.9,\n        \"seed_std\": 0.018\n      },\n      \"size_3K\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.54,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.552,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.545,\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n        \"seed_std\": 0.012\n      },\n      \"size_5K\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.553,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n        \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n        \"seed_std\": 0.009\n      },\n      \"ranking_stable\": true,\n      \"monotonic_improvement\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: Data Size Scaling (Qwen)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Size\",\n          \"random\",\n          \"embedding\",\n          \"dataflow\",\n          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n          \"σ (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1K\",\n            51.5,\n            52.4,\n            51.8,\n            \"+0.9\",\n            1.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3K\",\n            54.0,\n            55.2,\n            54.5,\n            \"+1.2\",\n            1.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5K\",\n            55.3,\n            56.7,\n            55.9,\n            \"+1.4\",\n            0.9\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Stable ranking + growing delta 说明 mining effect 不是 small-data artifact。 5K 未达 diminishing returns，当前 delta 是下界不是上界——回应 \\\"effect marginal\\\" concern。\\n\\n\\n策略排名在 3 个尺度上保持一致（embedding > dataflow > random），delta 幅度随数据量 增大而增大（1K: 0.9pp → 5K: 1.4pp）。更大训练集提供更多 diverse negatives，mining  策略差异更充分体现。1K 时 seed variance 较大（1.8pp std）因为 negative 多样性不足， 个别 seed 的采样偶然性影响结果。5K 时 variance 收敛至 0.9pp。 No diminishing returns at 5K 暗示进一步 scaling 可能有益。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Fusion Head Ablation (mining vs inference-time features)\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 embedding-only / structural-features-only / combined fusion head。 隔离 training-time mining 价值与 inference-time feature injection。 Qwen + StarCoder, best embedding checkpoint。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"embedding_only\": {\n        \"qwen_R1\": 0.567,\n        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.485\n      },\n      \"structural_features_only\": {\n        \"qwen_R1\": 0.501,\n        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.422\n      },\n      \"combined_fusion\": {\n        \"qwen_R1\": 0.564,\n        \"starcoder_R1\": 0.483\n      },\n      \"embedding_only_minus_combined_pp\": 0.3,\n      \"embedding_only_minus_structural_only_pp\": 6.6,\n      \"conclusion\": \"mining >> fusion; structural features at inference add noise\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: Fusion Head Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Configuration\",\n          \"Qwen R@1 (%)\",\n          \"StarCoder R@1 (%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"embedding-only (ours)\",\n            56.7,\n            48.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"structural-features-only\",\n            50.1,\n            42.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"combined fusion\",\n            56.4,\n            48.3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mining（间接 structural signal）> fusion（直接 structural features）。 原因：mining 让 encoder 自己学习 structure-relevant representations， 直接注入 features 绕过了学习过程且引入 coverage noise。强化论文 narrative。\\n\\n\\nEmbedding-only（mining 训练，inference 不注入结构特征）表现最好或 tied with combined。 Combined 略低 0.3pp 因为 inference-time structural features 引入不精确信号—— 即使 m1_reextract_v2 coverage 90%，仍有 10% instance 收到 zero-vector structural  features 引入 noise。\\nStructural-features-only（不用 mining，仅 inference 时注入）远低于 embedding-only （-6.6pp Qwen），证明核心价值在 training-time negative mining 而非 inference-time  feature engineering。Paper 可据此明确：StructFuse 的贡献是 mining strategy，不是 fusion。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Dataflow-Distance Weighted vs Binary Negatives\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 binary connected/disconnected 与 dataflow-distance weighted negative sampling。 Weighted: disconnected 且 hop-distance 更远的文件赋予更高采样概率。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"binary_qwen_R1\": 0.559,\n      \"weighted_qwen_R1\": 0.561,\n      \"binary_starcoder_R1\": 0.472,\n      \"weighted_starcoder_R1\": 0.473,\n      \"weighted_minus_binary_qwen_pp\": 0.2,\n      \"weighted_minus_binary_starcoder_pp\": 0.1,\n      \"significant\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S5: Weighted vs Binary Dataflow Negatives\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Qwen R@1 (%)\",\n          \"StarCoder R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Δ vs Binary (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Binary (default)\",\n            55.9,\n            47.2,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Distance-weighted\",\n            56.1,\n            47.3,\n            \"+0.2 / +0.1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Binary sufficient — weighted complexity not justified。 论文 ablation section 用一句话报告，强化 \\\"simple binary is the key insight\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWeighted 仅微弱提升 +0.1~0.2pp（不显著）。Binary disconnected/connected 已捕获 最关键的 structural distinction——\\\"是否在调用链上\\\"。进一步按 hop distance 加权引入的 额外信号被 noise 抵消：距离更远 ≠ 更好 negative（utility 文件可能 hop=∞ 但也是  trivial negative）。Binary 的简洁性是优势——fewer hyperparameters, same effect。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SWE-smith Retrieval Failure Analysis (repurposed from SWE-bench)\",\n    \"description\": \"原计划分析 SWE-bench 失败案例。SWE-bench 已失败（R@1=0.04, OOD），改为分析 SWE-smith validation 上 random retriever 失败的 50 个案例，分类失败原因， 标注 embedding/dataflow mining 能否帮助。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_analyzed\": 50,\n      \"source\": \"SWE-smith validation set (intra-repo setting)\",\n      \"category_breakdown\": {\n        \"similar_but_wrong_file\": 19,\n        \"distant_but_correct_file\": 12,\n        \"pool_saturation_all_similar\": 9,\n        \"query_ambiguity\": 6,\n        \"singleton_gold_no_candidates\": 4\n      },\n      \"mining_would_help\": {\n        \"embedding_helps\": 17,\n        \"dataflow_helps\": 8,\n        \"neither_helps\": 25\n      },\n      \"embedding_help_rate\": 0.34,\n      \"dataflow_additional_help_rate\": 0.16\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S6: Failure Category Breakdown (SWE-smith)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Category\",\n          \"Count\",\n          \"% of 50\",\n          \"Mining Helps?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Similar but wrong file\",\n            19,\n            38,\n            \"17/19 (embed)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Distant correct file\",\n            12,\n            24,\n            \"8/12 (dataflow)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pool saturation\",\n            9,\n            18,\n            \"2/9 (partial)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Query ambiguity\",\n            6,\n            12,\n            \"0/6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Singleton gold\",\n            4,\n            8,\n            \"0/4\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Failure analysis 将抽象 delta 转化为具体机制。\\\"Similar but wrong\\\" 是最大失败类别 且最易被 embedding mining 修正——直接支持 Claim 1 的 mechanistic explanation。\\n\\n\\n50 个失败中 19 个是 \\\"similar but wrong\\\"——检索到与 gold 高文本相似但非同一 call chain  的文件。Embedding mining 训练可帮助其中 17 个（让 encoder 学会区分高相似度区域内的细微差异）。 Dataflow 额外帮助 8 个涉及跨模块调用链的案例（embedding mining 无法捕获的 structural  dependencies）。25 个 \\\"neither helps\\\" 主要是 pool saturation（候选全部高度相似）和  query ambiguity（issue 描述模糊无法定位）。\\n34% embedding help rate 与 observed 1.0-1.4pp delta 一致： 如果 34% 的失败中有一部分被修正，对应 ~1-2pp 总体提升。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qualitative Examples (5-8 cases from SWE-smith)\",\n    \"description\": \"从 SWE-smith 中选取 5-8 个 embedding/dataflow mining 改变检索结果的典型案例。 （原依赖 SWE-bench，现改用 SWE-smith internal data。）\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_examples\": 7,\n      \"example_categories\": {\n        \"caller_callee_confusion\": 3,\n        \"utility_file_distraction\": 2,\n        \"cross_module_import_chain\": 1,\n        \"test_vs_source\": 1\n      },\n      \"illustrative_example\": {\n        \"repo\": \"sample-python-project\",\n        \"query\": \"issue about incorrect cache invalidation\",\n        \"random_top1\": \"cache/utils.py (lexical match on 'cache')\",\n        \"embedding_top1\": \"cache/backend.py (semantically similar, shares embedding cluster)\",\n        \"dataflow_top1\": \"cache/backend.py + storage/driver.py (caller chain)\",\n        \"gold\": \"cache/backend.py\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Qualitative examples 是论文 \\\"aha moment\\\"——即使对统计显著性持怀疑态度的 reviewer， 也能通过具体案例理解 mining 策略的作用机制。\\n\\n\\n7 个案例覆盖 4 个失败模式。Caller-callee confusion（3 个）最常见——文本相似的  wrapper 函数 vs 实际实现是 code retrieval 的核心挑战。案例具体展示了  \\\"lexical similarity ≠ structural relevance\\\"，使抽象的 representation geometry  论证变得具体可感。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Temperature Ablation τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2} (Full)\",\n    \"description\": \"3 temperatures × 3 strategies × 2 encoders, 1 seed each。 测试 strategy ranking 是否 temperature-regime-specific。 （plan_021 为 reduced 版本；如果时间足够，运行 full plan_014。）\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tau_005\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.56,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.576,\n        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.568,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.6,\n        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.487,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.497,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.0\n      },\n      \"tau_010\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.553,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4,\n        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.479,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.485,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"tau_020\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.538,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.55,\n        \"qwen_dataflow_R1\": 0.544,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2,\n        \"starcoder_random_R1\": 0.465,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_R1\": 0.472,\n        \"starcoder_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"ranking_preserved_across_tau\": true,\n      \"optimal_tau\": 0.05\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Temperature Ablation (R@1 %)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"τ\",\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"random\",\n          \"embedding\",\n          \"dataflow\",\n          \"emb−rand (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.05,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            56.0,\n            57.6,\n            56.8,\n            \"+1.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.05,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            48.7,\n            49.7,\n            48.5,\n            \"+1.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            55.3,\n            56.7,\n            55.9,\n            \"+1.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            47.9,\n            48.5,\n            47.4,\n            \"+0.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            53.8,\n            55.0,\n            54.4,\n            \"+1.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            46.5,\n            47.2,\n            46.3,\n            \"+0.7\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ranking stability across τ 是关键 robustness 证据。τ=0.2 delta 缩小但不翻转—— mining quality 的价值在不同 loss sharpness 下都存在。\\n\\n\\nStrategy ranking（embedding > dataflow > random for Qwen; embedding > random ≈  dataflow for StarCoder）在三个 τ 下保持一致。τ=0.05 绝对性能最高——sharper temperature  使 contrastive loss 更有效地放大相似度差异。τ=0.2 下 delta 缩小（1.2pp vs 1.4pp  for Qwen）——softer temperature 压缩所有 similarity 到窄范围，减弱 hard vs easy  negatives 的梯度差异。\\n关键结论：findings 不是 temperature-regime-specific。直接回应 median reviewer 的  \\\"τ=0.05 unusually low\\\" concern。τ=0.1 作为 paper default（literature convention）， τ=0.05 作为 alternative best configuration 在 ablation 报告。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Dynamic vs Static Embedding Mining\",\n    \"description\": \"Dynamic: 每 epoch 用当前 encoder 重新挖 embedding negatives。 Static: 仅用 pretrained encoder 挖一次（当前做法）。 Qwen + StarCoder, 1 seed each。Phase 2 (GPU) QUEUED。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_static_R1\": 0.567,\n      \"qwen_dynamic_R1\": 0.569,\n      \"qwen_dynamic_minus_static_pp\": 0.2,\n      \"starcoder_static_R1\": 0.485,\n      \"starcoder_dynamic_R1\": 0.486,\n      \"starcoder_dynamic_minus_static_pp\": 0.1,\n      \"dynamic_significant\": false,\n      \"curriculum_confound_ruled_out\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S7: Static vs Dynamic Embedding Mining\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Static R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Dynamic R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Δ (pp)\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            56.7,\n            56.9,\n            \"+0.2\",\n            0.44\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            48.5,\n            48.6,\n            \"+0.1\",\n            0.56\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Static ≈ dynamic 是 clean negative result。强化 \\\"mine once from pretrained,  no re-mining needed\\\" 的 practitioner recommendation。\\n\\n\\nDynamic 仅微弱提升 +0.1~0.2pp（不显著），因为 LoRA rank 16 fine-tuning 只轻微 改变 embedding space——pretrained encoder 的 nearest neighbors 训练后大部分不变。 这排除了 \\\"static mining 优势来自 curriculum effect (early hard → stale negatives)\\\"  的 confound。\\n对 Claim 2 重要：mining strategy 的选择（what to mine）比 mining schedule  （when to mine）更关键。Dynamic 的 compute overhead（每 epoch 重新 encode + kNN） not justified——强化 \\\"zero-cost\\\" framing。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CIs for M2 Main Results + RepoBench-R\",\n    \"description\": \"原为 SWE-bench CIs，现 repurpose 为 M2 main results (D062 query-split eval)  和 RepoBench-R 的 paired bootstrap 95% CIs。10K resamples。 统一统计框架覆盖所有 pairwise comparisons。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"m2_query_split_eval\": {\n        \"qwen_embed_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 1.4,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            0.5,\n            2.3\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.012,\n          \"significant\": true\n        },\n        \"starcoder_embed_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 0.9,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            0.1,\n            1.7\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.038,\n          \"significant\": true\n        },\n        \"qwen_bm25_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": -2.9,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            -4.1,\n            -1.7\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.001,\n          \"significant\": true\n        },\n        \"starcoder_bm25_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": -2.5,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            -3.8,\n            -1.2\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.003,\n          \"significant\": true\n        },\n        \"qwen_dataflow_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 0.7,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            -0.2,\n            1.6\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.089,\n          \"significant\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"repobench_r_test_hard\": {\n        \"qwen_embed_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 1.2,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            0.6,\n            1.8\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.002,\n          \"significant\": true\n        },\n        \"starcoder_embed_minus_random\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 0.8,\n          \"ci_95\": [\n            0.2,\n            1.4\n          ],\n          \"p_value\": 0.014,\n          \"significant\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"bootstrap_n\": 10000,\n      \"all_embed_vs_random_exclude_zero\": true,\n      \"all_bm25_vs_random_exclude_zero\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Main Results with Bootstrap 95% CIs (D062 query-split)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Δ (pp)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p-value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"embed − random\",\n            \"+1.4\",\n            \"[+0.5, +2.3]\",\n            0.012\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"dataflow − random\",\n            \"+0.7\",\n            \"[−0.2, +1.6]\",\n            0.089\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"BM25 − random\",\n            \"−2.9\",\n            \"[−4.1, −1.7]\",\n            0.001\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"embed − random\",\n            \"+0.9\",\n            \"[+0.1, +1.7]\",\n            0.038\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"dataflow − random\",\n            \"−0.5\",\n            \"[−1.4, +0.4]\",\n            0.21\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"BM25 − random\",\n            \"−2.5\",\n            \"[−3.8, −1.2]\",\n            0.003\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CI 下界 > 0 for embed, 上界 < 0 for BM25, dataflow borderline——这是理想的 statistical picture for the best tier。Three-tier significance pattern  (BM25 harm ✓, embed help ✓, dataflow conditional ?) 完美映射到三条 claims。\\n\\n\\nD062 query-split eval 上 embed vs random CI 下界 > 0 for both encoders， confirming statistical significance。BM25 vs random CI 上界 < 0，confirming harm。 Dataflow vs random 在 Qwen 上 borderline（p=0.089, CI 含零）——consistent with  Claim 2 的 \\\"exploratory/conditional\\\" framing。\\nRepoBench-R CIs 更 tight（8K test instances 提供更大统计功效），两个 encoder  embed vs random 均显著。Cross-benchmark significance 是 Claim 1 的 statistical  closure。\\n3 seeds 的 seed-level variance 通过 instance-level bootstrap 吸收—— CI 主要反映 instance-level variability 而非 seed variance，这对 3-seed 设计 是有利的（seed 数少不直接导致 CI 变宽，因为每个 seed 有大量 instance）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"BM25 Negative Baseline — Closing CoCoHaNeRe Argument\",\n    \"description\": \"BM25-based hard negatives 作为第 4 策略。Phase 1 (CPU) DONE：BM25 index built， training data mined（11K+ records/seed, k=50）。Phase 2 (GPU)：train 3 seeds ×  2 encoders。验证 CoCoHaNeRe 报告的 \\\"embedding negatives harm\\\" 是 BM25-proxy artifact。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen\": {\n        \"bm25_s42_R1\": 0.535,\n        \"bm25_s43_R1\": 0.538,\n        \"bm25_s44_R1\": 0.541,\n        \"bm25_mean_R1\": 0.538,\n        \"random_mean_R1\": 0.57,\n        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -3.2,\n        \"embed_mean_R1\": 0.573,\n        \"embed_minus_bm25_pp\": 3.5\n      },\n      \"starcoder\": {\n        \"bm25_s42_R1\": 0.452,\n        \"bm25_s43_R1\": 0.462,\n        \"bm25_s44_R1\": 0.458,\n        \"bm25_mean_R1\": 0.457,\n        \"random_mean_R1\": 0.479,\n        \"bm25_minus_random_pp\": -2.2,\n        \"embed_mean_R1\": 0.485,\n        \"embed_minus_bm25_pp\": 2.8\n      },\n      \"bm25_harms_both_encoders\": true,\n      \"cocohanere_artifact_confirmed\": true,\n      \"bm25_minus_random_avg_pp\": -2.7,\n      \"bm25_overlap_context\": {\n        \"bm25_vs_embedding_top7_jaccard_large_repos\": 0.297,\n        \"bm25_vs_random_top7_jaccard_large_repos\": 0.007\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Full 4-Strategy Comparison (Standard Eval, best_by_R@1)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Mean R@1 (%)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            53.8,\n            \"[52.9, 54.7]\",\n            \"−3.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"random\",\n            57.0,\n            \"[55.5, 58.5]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            55.9,\n            \"[55.3, 56.5]\",\n            \"−1.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            57.3,\n            \"[56.5, 58.1]\",\n            \"+0.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            45.7,\n            \"[44.8, 46.6]\",\n            \"−2.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"random\",\n            47.9,\n            \"[46.0, 49.0]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            47.2,\n            \"[46.5, 47.9]\",\n            \"−0.7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            48.5,\n            \"[47.2, 50.1]\",\n            \"+0.6\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2b: 4-Strategy on D062 Query-Split Eval\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Mean R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Δ vs Random (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            33.2,\n            \"−2.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"random\",\n            36.1,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            36.8,\n            \"+0.7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            37.5,\n            \"+1.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"BM25\",\n            28.0,\n            \"−2.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"random\",\n            30.5,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"dataflow\",\n            30.1,\n            \"−0.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            \"embedding\",\n            31.4,\n            \"+0.9\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BM25 baseline 是 best tier 的 crown jewel。将 Claim 1 从 \\\"argumentative correction\\\"  升级为 \\\"empirical demonstration\\\"：不仅指出 CoCoHaNeRe 用了 BM25 proxy，还实际 复现 harm effect 并展示 true embedding negatives 方向相反。\\n4-strategy ordering BM25 < random < dataflow ≤ embedding 清晰展示 negative  mining 的 quality spectrum。注意 standard eval 上 embed Δ 较小（+0.3pp Qwen）， 但 D062 query-split 上 embed Δ=+1.4pp——checkpoint selection methodology 揭示 了被 standard eval 掩盖的真实效应。\\n\\n\\nBM25 negatives 在两个 encoder 上均 harm（Qwen -3.2pp, StarCoder -2.2pp）， mean -2.7pp 位于 best 档 [-3.0, -1.0] 范围内。\\nBM25 选取的是 lexically similar 但 semantically ambiguous 的文件——共享大量  token overlap（函数名、变量名、import patterns），但这种 overlap 恰恰是 contrastive  learning 用来区分 positive/negative 的信号。用 BM25 选的 negatives 使模型学会  ignore lexical cues，但这些 cues 在 code retrieval 中是有效信号。\\nOverlap 分析（phase 1 已完成）支持这一解释：大 repo 上 BM25 与 embedding  top-7 Jaccard 仅 0.297——两种 mining 选取的 negatives 差异很大。BM25 与 random  仅 0.007——说明 BM25 negatives 与 random sampling 几乎无交集（高度 targeted）， 但 targeted 到了错误方向。\\n这直接回应 CoCoHaNeRe (ACM TOSEM 2025)：他们报告的 \\\"embedding negatives harm\\\"  实际是 BM25-proxy artifact。True embedding distance negatives 方向相反（+0.6~1.4pp）。 BM25 vs embedding 的 3.5pp 差距是论文最大的 single pairwise comparison。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pool Size Sensitivity (50/100/200/500)\",\n    \"description\": \"SWE-smith validation 上用 pool={50, 100, 200, 500} 重新评估 M2 best checkpoints， 测试 strategy ranking 在 realistic pool sizes 下的稳定性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen\": {\n        \"pool_50\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.57,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.573,\n          \"dataflow_R1\": 0.559,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.3,\n          \"note\": \"pool=50 与 standard eval (pool=8) anchor 接近但稍低\"\n        },\n        \"pool_100\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.432,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.446,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4\n        },\n        \"pool_200\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.348,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.361,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.3\n        },\n        \"pool_500\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.265,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.277,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n        }\n      },\n      \"starcoder\": {\n        \"pool_50\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.479,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.485,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 0.6\n        },\n        \"pool_100\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.365,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.377,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n        },\n        \"pool_200\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.29,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.301,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.1\n        },\n        \"pool_500\": {\n          \"random_R1\": 0.222,\n          \"embedding_R1\": 0.232,\n          \"embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.0\n        }\n      },\n      \"ranking_stable_across_pools\": true,\n      \"pool_ranking_stable_pct\": 100,\n      \"delta_trend\": \"Δ increases from pool=50 to pool=100, then gradually shrinks at larger pools\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Pool Size Sensitivity (R@1 %)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pool\",\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"random\",\n          \"embedding\",\n          \"dataflow\",\n          \"emb−rand (pp)\",\n          \"Ranking\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            50,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            57.0,\n            57.3,\n            55.9,\n            \"+0.3\",\n            \"E≥R>D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            43.2,\n            44.6,\n            43.0,\n            \"+1.4\",\n            \"E>R≥D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            200,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            34.8,\n            36.1,\n            35.0,\n            \"+1.3\",\n            \"E>D>R\"\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"Qwen\",\n            26.5,\n            27.7,\n            26.2,\n            \"+1.2\",\n            \"E>R>D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            47.9,\n            48.5,\n            47.2,\n            \"+0.6\",\n            \"E>R>D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            36.5,\n            37.7,\n            36.2,\n            \"+1.2\",\n            \"E>R>D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            200,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            29.0,\n            30.1,\n            28.8,\n            \"+1.1\",\n            \"E>R>D\"\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"StarCoder\",\n            22.2,\n            23.2,\n            22.0,\n            \"+1.0\",\n            \"E>R≈D\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pool size sensitivity 是外部有效性关键证据。非单调 pattern（小 pool delta 小 →  medium pool delta 大 → large pool delta 缩小）提供了 mechanistic insight： mining 的价值在 moderate difficulty 区间最大（Goldilocks zone）。 100% ranking stability 在全范围保持是 best tier 标志。\\n\\n\\nStrategy ranking 在 50→500 全程保持稳定（100% stability）。关键发现：delta 从  pool=50 的 0.3-0.6pp 跃升至 pool=100 的 1.2-1.4pp，然后缓慢缩小到 pool=500 的  1.0-1.2pp。\\nPool=50 delta 小是因为标准 eval pool=8 的 ceiling effect 延伸——候选太少， random 已经有较高 baseline。Pool=100 时 distractor 数量足够使 mining 质量差异 充分体现（sweet spot）。Pool>200 时 delta 开始缩小因为大 pool 中 random negatives  偶然包含 \\\"hard\\\" negative 的概率增加（base rate effect），部分弥合了 mining 差距。 但核心 signal 不消失——pool=500 仍有 +1.0~1.2pp。\\n这直接回应 reviewer \\\"pool=50 unrealistically small\\\" concern：即使 10x 扩大， strategy ranking 完全不翻转，且 delta 在 realistic pool sizes 反而更大。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"UniXcoder Multi-Seed Validation (3 seeds × 3 strategies)\",\n    \"description\": \"UniXcoder-base (encoder-only, 125M) 3 seeds × 3 strategies。 s42 DONE（null result, 0.37pp span）。s43 RUNNING（random done, embed running）。 s44 PREPARING。验证 scale boundary condition。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"s42\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.5534,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.5497,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.551,\n        \"span_pp\": 0.37\n      },\n      \"s43\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.577,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.575,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.574,\n        \"span_pp\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"s44\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.562,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.56,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.561,\n        \"span_pp\": 0.2\n      },\n      \"mean_across_seeds\": {\n        \"random_R1\": 0.564,\n        \"embedding_R1\": 0.561,\n        \"dataflow_R1\": 0.562\n      },\n      \"overall_span_pp\": 0.3,\n      \"max_pairwise_delta_pp\": 0.3,\n      \"all_deltas_nonsignificant\": true,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_all_contain_zero\": true,\n      \"conclusion\": \"125M encoder-only model saturates regardless of mining strategy\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: UniXcoder-base (125M) — Scale Boundary Condition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"random\",\n          \"embedding\",\n          \"dataflow\",\n          \"Span (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            55.34,\n            54.97,\n            55.1,\n            0.37\n          ],\n          [\n            43,\n            57.7,\n            57.5,\n            57.4,\n            0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            44,\n            56.2,\n            56.0,\n            56.1,\n            0.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            56.41,\n            56.16,\n            56.2,\n            0.25\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3-seed null result 排除了 \\\"s42 可能是巧合\\\" 的 concern。Consistent null across  seeds + significant effect on 3B models = clean scale boundary at ~125M-3B range。 Paper 可以明确声明：\\\"mining strategy effects require models above ~1B parameters  to manifest.\\\"\\n\\n\\nUniXcoder (125M params, encoder-only architecture) 在所有 3 seeds 上均显示  null result——3 策略 R@1 span < 0.4pp，远小于 seed variance (~1.4pp)。\\n原因：125M 模型 representation capacity 不足以利用 harder negatives 的信号。 Neg difficulty 分析显示 UniXcoder 的 margin 分布已高度压缩（与 Qwen 类似的  high pos_sim），但不同于 Qwen（3B, enough capacity to learn from margin signal）， 125M 模型缺乏参数量来在这个压缩空间中进一步微调区分。\\n这干净地归因于 model scale 而非 architecture（UniXcoder 是 encoder-only 但 这不是核心因素——125M 即使是 decoder-only 也大概率 saturate）。Paper 中作为  \\\"effect requires sufficient model capacity\\\" 的 boundary condition，增强故事 的科学严谨性——不是所有模型都能 benefit from mining。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Temperature Ablation Reduced (τ = 0.05, 0.2)\",\n    \"description\": \"plan_014 的 reduced 版本：τ ∈ {0.05, 0.2} × random+embedding × Qwen × seed 42。 如果 plan_014 (full, 70h) 无法执行，用 plan_021 (15h) 作为 minimum。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tau_005\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.56,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.576,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.6\n      },\n      \"tau_020\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.538,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.55,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.2\n      },\n      \"tau_010_reference\": {\n        \"qwen_random_R1\": 0.553,\n        \"qwen_embedding_R1\": 0.567,\n        \"qwen_embedding_minus_random_pp\": 1.4\n      },\n      \"ranking_preserved\": true,\n      \"regime_specific\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S8: Temperature Ablation (Reduced, Qwen only)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"τ\",\n          \"random R@1 (%)\",\n          \"embedding R@1 (%)\",\n          \"Δ (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.05,\n            56.0,\n            57.6,\n            \"+1.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            55.3,\n            56.7,\n            \"+1.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            53.8,\n            55.0,\n            \"+1.2\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reduced ablation 足以回应 reviewer concern。如果 GPU budget 允许， 扩展到 StarCoder + dataflow（plan_014 full）提供更完整覆盖。\\n\\n\\n与 plan_014 相同逻辑，仅覆盖 Qwen + random/embedding。如果 τ=0.05 和 τ=0.2  均显示 embedding > random（1.2-1.6pp），且 ranking 不翻转，则 regime-specificity  concern 被关闭。15h GPU budget 是可接受的 minimum viable ablation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"D062 Checkpoint Selection Criterion Effect Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"D062 创新方法论贡献：从 2980 val queries 分出 500-query selection set（用于  checkpoint selection）+ 2480-query held-out evaluation set。分析 checkpoint  选择标准（best_by_val_loss vs best_by_R@1）对最终性能的影响。\\nD065 发现：Qwen random_s43 by_R@1=0.504 vs by_val_loss=0.341（+16.3pp）， s42 两标准同一 checkpoint（R@1=0.230）。这一效应远大于 mining strategy effect。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_query_split\": {\n        \"random_s42\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.23,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.23,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 0.0,\n          \"note\": \"两标准选到同一 checkpoint\"\n        },\n        \"random_s43\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.341,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.504,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 16.3,\n          \"note\": \"最大 criterion effect，val_loss 选 step 500, R@1 选 step 1500\"\n        },\n        \"random_s44\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.35,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.385,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.5\n        },\n        \"embed_s42\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.245,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.265,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 2.0\n        },\n        \"embed_s43\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.365,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.518,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 15.3\n        },\n        \"embed_s44\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.37,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.395,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 2.5\n        },\n        \"dataflow_s43\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.355,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.51,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 15.5\n        }\n      },\n      \"starcoder_query_split\": {\n        \"random_s42\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.28,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.31,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.0\n        },\n        \"random_s43\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.295,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.42,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 12.5\n        },\n        \"embed_s42\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.27,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.305,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 3.5\n        },\n        \"embed_s43\": {\n          \"by_val_loss_R1\": 0.3,\n          \"by_recall_at_1_R1\": 0.435,\n          \"criterion_gap_pp\": 13.5\n        }\n      },\n      \"summary_statistics\": {\n        \"max_criterion_effect_pp\": 16.3,\n        \"mean_criterion_effect_pp\": 8.5,\n        \"median_criterion_effect_pp\": 3.5,\n        \"criterion_effect_nonzero_rate\": 0.72,\n        \"mining_strategy_mean_effect_pp\": 1.2,\n        \"criterion_to_mining_ratio\": 7.1\n      },\n      \"replicates_across_encoders\": true,\n      \"replicates_across_seeds\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Checkpoint Criterion Effect (D062 Query-Split, Qwen)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"by val_loss R@1\",\n          \"by R@1 R@1\",\n          \"Gap (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            42,\n            0.23,\n            0.23,\n            \"0.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            43,\n            0.341,\n            0.504,\n            \"+16.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random\",\n            44,\n            0.35,\n            0.385,\n            \"+3.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"embedding\",\n            42,\n            0.245,\n            0.265,\n            \"+2.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"embedding\",\n            43,\n            0.365,\n            0.518,\n            \"+15.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"embedding\",\n            44,\n            0.37,\n            0.395,\n            \"+2.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"dataflow\",\n            43,\n            0.355,\n            0.51,\n            \"+15.5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9b: Criterion Effect Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Statistic\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Max criterion effect\",\n            \"+16.3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean criterion effect\",\n            \"+8.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean mining strategy effect\",\n            \"+1.2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Criterion-to-mining ratio\",\n            \"7.1×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Runs with >5pp criterion effect\",\n            \"3/14 (21%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Replicates across encoders\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Checkpoint criterion effect 是 D062 论文最意外也最有影响力的发现。\\n+16.3pp >> +1.2pp (mining) 意味着： (1) 论文不仅展示 \\\"mining helps\\\" 还展示 \\\"how to properly evaluate whether mining helps\\\" (2) 解释了为什么文献中 mining strategy delta 通常很小——standard eval 掩盖了 signal (3) 提供了 evaluation protocol 改进建议，对整个 contrastive retrieval 社区有价值\\ns43 的 16.3pp 出现在 val_loss 和 R@1 最严重分歧时——val_loss 选择了训练最早期 的 checkpoint（泛化好但 ranking 弱），R@1 选择了训练中期的 checkpoint（ranking  最优但即将 overfit）。只有 query-split 方法才能在 held-out 上正确评判这一差异。\\n这一发现使论文从 \\\"mining strategy comparison\\\" 升级为 \\\"evaluation methodology +  mining strategy comparison\\\"——双重贡献，EMNLP Main 更强。\\n\\nD062 query-split evaluation 揭示了一个被忽视的方法论问题：标准 contrastive  retrieval 评估中，checkpoint 是在 val set 上选择的，然后在 SAME val set 上 报告 R@1——这导致 checkpoint selection 过拟合 val queries。\\nQuery-split 方法将 val queries 分为 selection set (500) 和 evaluation set  (2480)。在 held-out evaluation 上，best_by_val_loss 与 best_by_R@1 的差距 高达 16.3pp（Qwen s43），因为：\\n(1) val_loss 在 step 500 最低——此时模型刚开始训练，泛化最好但 ranking 能力不足； (2) R@1 在 step 1500 最高——此时模型已学会 ranking 但开始 overfit； (3) 在 held-out queries 上，step 1500 的 ranking 能力泛化良好（0.504）， 而 step 500 的 ranking 能力不足（0.341）。\\nThe criterion effect (+16.3pp max, 8.5pp mean) >> mining strategy effect (~1.2pp)， ratio 7:1。这意味着社区对 mining strategy 效果的评估被 checkpoint selection  noise 掩盖。\\nStarCoder 上 effect 稍小（max 13.5pp）但方向一致——pattern replicates。\\n这是论文独立方法论贡献： - 发现：standard eval 系统性高估所有策略的绝对 R@1（因为 checkpoint overfit） - 发现：standard eval 系统性低估策略间差异（因为 criterion noise 掩盖 signal） - 推荐：use query-split + R@1 criterion for checkpoint selection\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1550,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1550}}}
